          "cookies": [],
          "content": {
            "size": 85571,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"data\":{\"jobs\":[{\"id\":\"e6ae17f0-83e6-438c-94e6-42823105329d\",\"source_id\":\"2409499276\",\"obfuscated_id\":41803137,\"title\":\"Software / Web Engineer\",\"organization\":\"Jobgether\",\"job_url\":\"https://jobs.lever.co/jobgether/0a6fa4f0-f79c-44e1-b309-a51e9c42696f\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-12T05:15:00.706573Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"BR\",\"BRA\",\"Brazil\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":true,\"company_id\":\"5b90c142-3285-46c7-a1f8-3863e3891578\",\"company_image_id\":\"74624ec93d814ffc9ec4561e5a4d316b\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"BRL\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":72000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":144000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"JavaScript\",\"TypeScript\",\"React\",\"Vue\",\"Angular\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"AWS\",\"CI/CD\",\"Git\",\"API Integration\",\"Web Security\",\"Automated Testing\",\"Performance Optimization\",\"Cloud Infrastructure\",\"Debugging\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"This position is listed on behalf of a partner company, who manages all applications and next steps. Our partner is looking for a Software / Web Engineer based in Brazil.\\nAs a Software / Web Engineer, you will build fast, accessible, and reliable web applications that deliver seamless experiences for users and creators. You will combine hands-on front-end development with production engineering, taking ownership of the entire software lifecycle, from implementation and testing to deployment and monitoring. Working with modern JavaScript and TypeScript frameworks, you will develop responsive interfaces, integrate APIs and authentication systems, and optimize application performance. You will collaborate closely with product, design, backend, security, QA, and platform engineering teams to deliver secure, maintainable solutions. You will also work with AWS infrastructure to improve deployment reliability, troubleshoot production issues, and strengthen continuous delivery practices. This remote opportunity offers meaningful technical ownership, exposure to cloud technologies, and the chance to make a measurable impact on product quality and operational excellence. You will leverage AI-assisted development tools while maintaining strong engineering judgment and accountability for every solution delivered.\\n\\\\n\\n\\nAccountabilities\\nDevelop responsive, accessible, and high-performing web applications and reusable UI components using modern JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, CSS, and front-end frameworks.\\nTranslate product requirements and design specifications into polished, production-ready interfaces that provide consistent experiences across supported browsers, devices, and screen sizes.\\nIntegrate APIs, authentication systems, analytics, and third-party services while following secure development practices and protecting user data.\\nOptimize front-end performance, usability, accessibility, and reliability by identifying bottlenecks and addressing technical issues.\\nTest critical user journeys across browsers, devices, and network conditions, implementing automated tests for essential functionality and workflows.\\nInvestigate browser compatibility issues, integration failures, and production incidents, identifying root causes and implementing preventive improvements.\\nDeploy and maintain web applications in AWS environments, collaborating with platform and site reliability engineering teams to ensure operational readiness.\\nManage application configurations and environment-specific settings, monitor application health and performance, and participate in deployment, rollback, and production-support processes.\\nContribute to reliable, repeatable CI/CD workflows and improve deployment automation, testing practices, and production monitoring.\\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code, participate in code reviews, follow engineering standards, and document technical decisions and operational procedures.\\nCollaborate with product, design, backend, QA, security, and platform engineering teams to coordinate delivery and resolve technical dependencies.\\nUse AI coding assistants and agentic development tools effectively while independently reviewing and validating generated code for correctness, security, reliability, accessibility, and maintainability.\\nProtect proprietary code, credentials, customer information, and other sensitive data when using AI-assisted development tools, remaining accountable for all delivered code.\\nEstablish baseline performance and reliability metrics, identify improvement opportunities, and deliver measurable enhancements to critical user journeys.\\nDuring the first 90 days, learn the existing architecture and AWS deployment processes, deliver an agreed web improvement, strengthen automated testing, validate deployment and rollback procedures, and establish a roadmap for ongoing improvements.\\nOver the following 12–18 months, improve application performance, accessibility, and production reliability; increase automated test coverage; reduce recurring defects; and enhance monitoring and deployment processes.\\nRequirements\\nAt least three years of professional experience developing and maintaining production web applications.\\nStrong knowledge of JavaScript and/or TypeScript, HTML, and CSS, with practical experience building modern web interfaces.\\nExperience with a contemporary front-end framework such as React, Vue, Angular, or an equivalent technology.\\nDemonstrated ability to build responsive, accessible, and user-friendly applications that perform consistently across browsers and devices.\\nHands-on experience integrating APIs, authentication systems, and third-party services.\\nKnowledge of browser security and common web application security practices, including protecting credentials and sensitive information.\\nExperience writing, maintaining, and executing automated tests for critical application functionality.\\nStrong proficiency with Git, version control workflows, code reviews, and CI/CD pipelines.\\nPractical experience deploying and troubleshooting web applications in AWS environments.\\nAn active AWS certification is required. AWS Certified Developer – Associate is preferred.\\nStrong debugging, analytical thinking, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to investigate production issues and identify root causes.\\nAbility to work independently, take ownership of technical deliverables, and collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams.\\nComfort using AI-assisted and agentic coding tools, with the ability to develop and maintain production code independently, validate AI-generated implementations, and identify potential security and reliability issues.\\nExcellent communication and documentation skills, with a commitment to engineering quality, continuous improvement, and shared technical standards.\\nNice to have:\\nExperience with AWS services such as ECS, S3, CloudFront, RDS, Lambda, CloudWatch, and IAM.\\nFamiliarity with infrastructure as code, deployment automation, and cloud operations.\\nExperience with web performance optimization, including Core Web Vitals.\\nKnowledge of accessibility standards and guidelines, such as WCAG.\\nExperience with observability platforms, application monitoring, and error-tracking tools.\\nBackground working on consumer-facing, social, creator, media, or subscription-based products.\\nExperience collaborating with mobile engineering teams to deliver consistent cross-platform experiences.\\nFamiliarity with product analytics, event tracking, and application instrumentation.\\nBenefits\\nCompetitive salary in USD, aligned with your skills and experience.\\nPaid time off to support work-life balance and personal well-being.\\nHealth insurance subsidy to help cover healthcare expenses.\\nAnnual salary reviews to recognize performance and professional growth.\\nPaid training and certifications to support continuous learning and technical development.\\nFully remote work arrangement, offering flexibility to work from Brazil.\\nHands-on experience with AWS cloud services, modern web technologies, and production engineering.\\nOwnership across the software development lifecycle, from building user-facing features to deploying, monitoring, and maintaining applications.\\nOpportunities to contribute to engineering standards, automation, application security, and continuous delivery improvements.\\nCollaboration with multidisciplinary engineering and product teams in a technology-driven environment.\\n\\n\\\\n\\nHow Jobgether works:\\nWe use an AI-powered matching process to ensure your application is reviewed quickly, objectively, and fairly against the role's core requirements. Our system identifies the top-fitting candidates, and this shortlist is then shared directly with the hiring company. The final decision and next steps (interviews, assessments) are managed by their internal team.\\nWe appreciate your interest and wish you the best!\\nWhy Apply Through Jobgether? \\nData Privacy Notice: By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Jobgether will process your personal data to evaluate your candidacy and share relevant information with the hiring employer. This processing is based on legitimate interest and pre-contractual measures under applicable data protection laws (including GDPR). You may exercise your rights (access, rectification, erasure, objection) at any time.\\n#LI-CL1\"},{\"id\":\"703f25e1-2ec4-418e-b348-7cf545760e33\",\"source_id\":\"2410000887\",\"obfuscated_id\":41841838,\"title\":\"Software Developer, Web\",\"organization\":\"Slice\",\"job_url\":\"https://slice.careers/careers-listing?gh_jid=8260907\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-12T17:17:54.447323Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"CA\",\"CAN\",\"Canada\",\"GB\",\"GBR\",\"IN, US\",\"IN, USA\",\"IN, United States\",\"Indiana, US\",\"Indiana, USA\",\"Indiana, United States\",\"Muncie, IN, US\",\"Muncie, IN, USA\",\"Muncie, IN, United States\",\"Muncie, Indiana, US\",\"Muncie, Indiana, USA\",\"Muncie, Indiana, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United Kingdom\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":true,\"company_id\":\"1dd4b45d-df52-f2ff-f9ab-a1ff2b0458b9\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1494278467/jiwjgzpxn1lc3lpm0i64.png\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"GBP\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":45000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"React\",\"TypeScript\",\"Front-end development\",\"Debugging\",\"Troubleshooting\",\"Accessibility\",\"Performance optimization\",\"SEO\",\"Test coverage\",\"API design\",\"System architecture\",\"Mentoring\",\"Coaching\",\"Continuous delivery\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Ilir Sela started Slice with the belief that local pizzerias deserve all of the advantages of major franchises without compromising their independence. Starting with his family’s pizzerias, we now empower over tens of thousands of restaurants with the technology, services, and collective power that owners need to better serve their digitally minded customers and build lasting businesses. We’re growing and adding more talent to help fulfil this valuable mission. That’s where you come in.\\nThe Role\\nTo continue scaling our Front-End teams we’re searching for an experienced software developer with a passion for Front-End development, particularly React and TypeScript. In this role, you will be instrumental in building world-class web products that empower small business owners.\\nYou will take a lead in solving technical challenges and utilise your expertise to contribute to and guide important technical decisions across the team. You’ll be challenged with consistent hands-on contributions both autonomously and as a group. Your experience will be valuable in partnering with the technical leads and Development Manager, allowing them to focus on wider team and strategic initiatives, while you pilot technical responsibilities. Your ability to troubleshoot complex production issues and ensure high-quality test coverage will be crucial to our continuous delivery model.\\nThe Team\\nYou’ll join a dynamic team of Front-End Developers and the individuals you'll collaborate with are curious, motivated, and exceptionally proficient in their respective domains. They welcome challenging tasks and thrive on resolving them within an empowered and supportive setting. Our team brings together talented developers from across the US, Canada, UK, and Eastern Europe, each contributing unique perspectives and expertise to drive success. We work on products used by hundreds of thousands of customers and we ship changes live to production every day. There are no direct reports for this position but you’ll be comfortable coaching and mentoring others, sharing knowledge and setting examples to the wider team.\\nThe Winning Recipe \\nWe’re looking for creative, entrepreneurial engineers who are excited to build world-class products for small business counters. These are the core competencies this role calls for:\\n3+ years experience building applications with React\\n3+ years experience with TypeScript - you view it as an invaluable tool and are an expert in its use\\nExcellent investigative debugging skills and a proven ability to troubleshoot complicated and subtle problems in high availability production environments\\nProven experience delivering web experiences that meet standards for accessibility, performance, and SEO\\nProficient on driving high quality and appropriate test coverage\\nYou are a Front-End specialist but you understand aspects of the full tech stack and can contribute meaningfully to API design and overall system architecture\\nThe Extras\\nWorking at Slice comes with a comprehensive set of benefits, but here are some of the unexpected highlights:\\nAccess to healthcare plans\\nFlexible working hours\\nGenerous time off policies\\nEmployee wellbeing allowance\\nMarket leading maternity and paternity schemes\\nThe Hiring Process\\nHere’s what you can expect from our hiring process if your candidacy progresses smoothly. We move quickly and strive for a fast turnaround from the final interview to the offer.\\n30 minute introductory meeting with your Recruiter\\n60 minute Live Coding Interview\\n60 minute Technical Interview\\n30 minute Hiring Manager meeting\\nOffer!\\nPizza brings people together. Slice is no different. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and embrace a diversity of backgrounds, cultures, and perspectives. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, age, or any other status protected by applicable national, federal, state, or local law. We are also proud members of the Diversity Mark NI initiative as a Bronze Member.\\nPrivacy Notice Statement of Acknowledgment\\nWhen you apply for a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected by Slice. Slice is keeping your data safe and secure. Once we have received your personal data, we put in place reasonable and appropriate measures and controls to prevent any accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, or unauthorised access. If selected, we will process your personal data for hiring /employment processes, as well as our legal obligations.\\nIf you are not selected for the job position and you have given consent on the question below (by selecting \\\"Give consent\\\") we will store and process your personal data and submitted documents (CV) to consider eligibility for employment up to 365 days (one year). You have the right to withdraw your previously given consent for storing your personal data and CV in the Slice database considering eligibility for employment for a year. You have the right to withdraw your consent at any time.\\nFor additional information and / or exercise of your rights to the protection of personal data, you can contact our Data Protection Officer, e-mail: privacy@slice.com\"},{\"id\":\"3a81188b-be75-485c-8e2b-5136582b868a\",\"source_id\":\"2421860169\",\"obfuscated_id\":42556854,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"LinTech Global\",\"job_url\":\"https://dexiangovernmentsolutions.applicantpro.com/jobs/4247615\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-19T18:23:19.446375Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"FL, US\",\"FL, USA\",\"FL, United States\",\"Florida, US\",\"Florida, USA\",\"Florida, United States\",\"Orlando, FL, US\",\"Orlando, FL, USA\",\"Orlando, FL, United States\",\"Orlando, Florida, US\",\"Orlando, Florida, USA\",\"Orlando, Florida, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"88c21b7f-c1c2-44aa-972c-b51b7bd83240\",\"company_image_id\":\"gxsrsy5s0vgodzauniej\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":110000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Microsoft Power Apps\",\"Power Automate\",\"Power BI\",\"SharePoint Online Administration\",\"Microsoft Dataverse\",\"Microsoft 365 Integration\",\"Solution Architecture\",\"Data Modeling\",\"Access Management\",\"Application Lifecycle Management\",\"Troubleshooting\",\"Root-Cause Analysis\",\"Security and Governance\",\"Requirements Analysis\",\"Technical Documentation\",\"Production Support\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Dexian Government Solutions is recruiting for a Software Developer to support our contract at CPE ST3 in Orlando, FL.\\nPosition Overview:\\nDexian Government Solutions is seeking an experienced, mid- to advanced-level Microsoft Power Platform and SharePoint Developer to design, deliver, administer, and support mission-focused business solutions. The primary focus is Microsoft Power Apps, Power Automate, Power BI, and SharePoint Online administration, with Dataverse and Microsoft 365 integrations as needed.\\nThe ideal candidate can independently own moderately complex to complex solutions from requirements through deployment and sustainment; administer SharePoint sites and access; diagnose cross-platform issues; and apply sound engineering judgment, security practices, governance, and documentation standards. This is a hands-on individual contributor role that works closely with business stakeholders and technical teams.\\nJob Duties:\\nDesign, develop, enhance, and sustain Power Apps solutions (Canvas and Model-Driven), including data connections, reusable components, and responsive user experiences.\\nArchitect, develop, and troubleshoot Power Automate cloud flows, approvals, notifications, integrations, and error-handling processes.\\nDesign and maintain Power BI reports, semantic models, dashboards, and data refresh processes to support business decisions.\\nPerform SharePoint Online administration, including site and site collection configuration, permissions and access management, lists, libraries, metadata, views, content organization, and lifecycle support.\\nImplement and support SharePoint-based business solutions integrated with Power Apps, Power Automate, Teams, and other Microsoft 365 services.\\nConfigure and maintain Dataverse tables, relationships, business rules, data models, and role-based security when required by the solution.\\nLead technical discovery, translate requirements into maintainable designs, provide effort estimates, and advise stakeholders on platform capabilities, constraints, and tradeoffs.\\nOwn troubleshooting, root-cause analysis, performance optimization, production support, and continuous improvement for existing solutions.\\nManage solution environments, connection references, deployment packages, version control, and application lifecycle management (ALM) practices consistent with organizational standards.\\nApply security, governance, least-privilege access, data protection, and change-management controls in a government or regulated environment.\\nCreate technical documentation, test plans, support procedures, and knowledge-transfer materials; collaborate with users and other IT teams throughout delivery and sustainment.\\nRequired Qualifications:\\nIAT II Certification, example Security+ certification, is Required to Start.\\nA DOD Secret Clearance is Required to Start.\\nFour or more years of relevant hands-on experience developing and supporting enterprise solutions with Microsoft Power Platform and/or SharePoint, including substantial recent experience with both.\\nDemonstrated proficiency with Power Apps, Power Automate, and Power BI, including integration, troubleshooting, and maintenance of production solutions.\\nHands-on SharePoint Online administration experience, including site management, permissions, lists/libraries, information architecture, and operational support.\\nExperience with Dataverse and/or SharePoint data sources, including data modeling, access controls, and integration approaches.\\nWorking knowledge of Microsoft 365 services and Power Platform environment management, solution packaging, deployment, and application lifecycle practices.\\nAbility to independently design and deliver moderately complex to complex solutions, resolve technical issues, and balance multiple priorities.\\nStrong technical communication, documentation, collaboration, and requirements-analysis skills with business and IT stakeholders.\\n\\nCompany Description\\nDexian Government Solutions is an award-winning, ISO 9001:2015 certified, business and GSA contract holder providing diversified Information Technology services to both Civilian and Defense agencies. Services include Software Development, Systems Integration, Data Management, Project Management, Operations \\u0026 Maintenance, Cybersecurity, and Training and Audio/Visual (AV) Solutions. Dexian Government Solutions has received several recognitions, including rankings on \\\"Top 50 Companies to Watch\\\", Washington Technology's Annual \\\"FAST 50\\\", and Inc. 500's List of \\\"Fastest Growing Private Companies\\\". The Dexian Government Solutions team is comprised of individuals who are dedicated to the success and sustainability of our customers and their missions. Our combination of technical expertise, big business experience, and small business agility allows us to promptly provide our customers with exceptional IT and engineering solutions.\\nBenefits\\nOur robust benefits package includes Open Paid Time Off, 11 Federal Paid Holidays \\u0026 5 Paid Sick Days, Company-paid Life/AD\\u0026D, Company-paid Short Term and Long-Term Disability, Health Insurance with Company Contribution, 401k Plan with Company Match, Employee Recognition Program, opportunity for Employee Referral Bonus, opportunity for annual Performance Bonus and much more!\\nEEO Statement\\nDexian Government Solutions is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All employment is decided based on qualifications, merit, and business need. \\nAll applicants will be considered for employment without attention to race, religion, color, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), marital status, genetic information (including characteristics and testing), gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, military and veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law in the locations where we operate.\\nIf you are an individual with a disability and would like to request a reasonable accommodation as part of the employment selection process, please contact Human Resources. The Company invites any applicant and/or employee to review the Company's written Affirmative Action Plan. This plan is available for inspection upon request.\\nhttp://Lintechglobal.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/poster_screen_reader_optimized.pdf\\n\\n#DICE\\n#LI-LM1\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nThis role requires an active Secret Security Clearance, customer approval, and successful completion of a pre-employment background screening.\"},{\"id\":\"4d493006-4cfc-438b-a1bc-ab0593d00a88\",\"source_id\":\"2415997257\",\"obfuscated_id\":42216914,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Tracsis\",\"job_url\":\"https://tracsis.careers.hibob.com/jobs/593acd9b-9329-4eda-bb22-b7db96c79ad3\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-15T17:19:37.525335Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"GB\",\"GBR\",\"London, GB\",\"London, GBR\",\"London, London, GB\",\"London, London, GBR\",\"London, London, United Kingdom\",\"London, United Kingdom\",\"United Kingdom\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"994906a0-7eb9-e580-b92c-876e54511eb9\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1472562591/qjybuh43xh5mxbg3vlmh.png\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"GBP\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":50000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":80000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Java\",\"Java EE\",\"Jakarta EE\",\"Spring Framework\",\"SQL\",\"Git\",\"Agile\",\"Maven\",\"Hibernate\",\"TypeScript\",\"JavaScript\",\"Angular\",\"CI/CD\",\"Docker\",\"Kubernetes\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Software Developer \\nHybrid - London  ( 1 day a week in office)\\nOur talented people are creating the technology of the future\\n\\nFrom scheduling to maintenance to keeping people safe, 2.7 million people are helped by our software daily. Technology makes it possible; people make it happen and you could be part of that. \\nThe Tracsis Group has grown rapidly, diversifying into related transport technologies, and successfully executing a strategy that has seen it make a total of seventeen acquisitions. \\nToday Tracsis is a leading provider of software, hardware, data analytics/GIS and services for the rail, traffic data and wider transport industries. The Group has c.500 permanent employees serving its growing customer base from offices in the UK, Ireland, the US and Germany. \\n\\nThe Role \\nJoin a collaborative and forward-thinking engineering team delivering technology that makes a real-world impact. As a Software Developer, you will play a key role in designing and building high-quality software solutions that support critical systems and services. \\nThis is an opportunity to take ownership of features from concept through to deployment, working alongside experienced engineers to solve complex problems and continuously improve the way software is built and delivered. You’ll contribute to scalable, secure and performant systems while continuing to develop your technical expertise in a supportive environment. \\n \\nWhat you will do \\n\\n * Design, develop and maintain software applications using modern technologies and frameworks\\n * Write clean, efficient and maintainable code aligned to engineering standards\\n * Contribute to the design of scalable, secure and high-performing systems\\n * Collaborate with team members through code reviews and shared best practices\\n * Investigate and resolve technical issues and performance challenges\\n * Translate business requirements into effective technical solutions\\n * Develop and execute unit, integration and system tests\\n * Contribute to documentation, knowledge sharing and team learning\\n * Participate in Agile ceremonies including sprint planning, stand-ups and retrospectives\\n * Build and enhance deployment processes and CI/CD pipelines\\n\\n \\nWhat We’re Looking For \\nRequired Skills \\n\\n * Experience building Java applications\\n * Familiarity with Java EE, Jakarta EE or the Spring Framework\\n * Comfortable writing SQL queries and interacting with relational databases\\n * Experience with Git (version control)\\n * Strong understanding of software development principles, data structures and algorithms\\n * Good knowledge of Agile methodologies and practices\\n * Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team\\n * Strong problem-solving and analytical skills\\n * Clear and effective communication skills\\n\\n \\nDesirable Skills \\n\\n * Maven\\n * Hibernate or other ORM frameworks\\n * TypeScript / JavaScript\\n * Angular\\n * CI/CD tools\\n * Docker / Kubernetes\\n * Experience working with distributed or cloud-based systems\\n\\n\\n \\nNext Steps \\nOur TA team are committed to responding to all candidates within a reasonable timeframe. \\nThe process: \\n\\n\\n 1. Call with our Talent Acquisition Team\\n 2. Light Technical Task \\n 3. Technical Task and Competency Based Questions\\n\\n\\nOur process is designed for us to understand your skills and experience and to give you the opportunity to find out more about the role, as well as the company.  \\nWe are committed to building a diverse workforce. Even if you do not tick all the boxes, we would still love to hear from you!  If you require any adjustments or additional support during the application and interview process do not hesitate to get in touch.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Our talented people are creating the technology of the future\",\"From scheduling to maintenance to keeping people safe, 2.7 million people are helped by our software daily. Technology makes it possible; people make it happen and you could be part of that.\",\"The Tracsis Group has grown rapidly, diversifying into related transport technologies, and successfully executing a strategy that has seen it make a total of seventeen acquisitions.\",\"Today Tracsis is a leading provider of software, hardware, data analytics/GIS and services for the rail, traffic data and wider transport industries. The Group has c.500 permanent employees serving its growing customer base from offices in the UK, Ireland, the US and Germany.\"],\"about_role\":\"Join a collaborative and forward-thinking engineering team delivering technology that makes a real-world impact. As a Software Developer, you will play a key role in designing and building high-quality software solutions that support critical systems and services. This is an opportunity to take ownership of features from concept through to deployment, working alongside experienced engineers to solve complex problems and continuously improve the way software is built and delivered. You’ll contribute to scalable, secure and performant systems while continuing to develop your technical expertise in a supportive environment.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[],\"education_level\":[],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"We are committed to building a diverse workforce. Even if you do not tick all the boxes, we would still love to hear from you! If you require any adjustments or additional support during the application and interview process do not hesitate to get in touch.\"],\"experience_level\":[],\"location\":[\"London\"],\"requirements\":[\"Experience building Java applications\",\"Familiarity with Java EE, Jakarta EE or the Spring Framework\",\"Comfortable writing SQL queries and interacting with relational databases\",\"Experience with Git (version control)\",\"Strong understanding of software development principles, data structures and algorithms\",\"Good knowledge of Agile methodologies and practices\",\"Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team\",\"Strong problem-solving and analytical skills\",\"Clear and effective communication skills\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Design, develop and maintain software applications using modern technologies and frameworks\",\"Write clean, efficient and maintainable code aligned to engineering standards\",\"Contribute to the design of scalable, secure and high-performing systems\",\"Collaborate with team members through code reviews and shared best practices\",\"Investigate and resolve technical issues and performance challenges\",\"Translate business requirements into effective technical solutions\",\"Develop and execute unit, integration and system tests\",\"Contribute to documentation, knowledge sharing and team learning\",\"Participate in Agile ceremonies including sprint planning, stand-ups and retrospectives\",\"Build and enhance deployment processes and CI/CD pipelines\"],\"skills\":[\"Maven\",\"Hibernate or other ORM frameworks\",\"TypeScript / JavaScript\",\"Angular\",\"CI/CD tools\",\"Docker / Kubernetes\",\"Experience working with distributed or cloud-based systems\"],\"work_type\":[\"Hybrid\"]}},{\"id\":\"109552bb-a105-4803-9bd9-2fc1e2b445d2\",\"source_id\":\"2413858972\",\"obfuscated_id\":42106557,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Esker\",\"job_url\":\"https://careers.esker.com/jobs/8139636-software-developer\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-14T18:23:38.889514Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Middleton, WI, US\",\"Middleton, WI, USA\",\"Middleton, WI, United States\",\"Middleton, Wisconsin, US\",\"Middleton, Wisconsin, USA\",\"Middleton, Wisconsin, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\",\"WI, US\",\"WI, USA\",\"WI, United States\",\"Wisconsin, US\",\"Wisconsin, USA\",\"Wisconsin, United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"5637a373-d7c5-27a2-2ab9-99d1350d8afe\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1397184873/177d41864d09ff4718ab8bac40d826ff.gif\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":90000,\"salary_max_value\":120000,\"salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":90000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":120000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"TypeScript\",\"JavaScript\",\"C#\",\"Python\",\"Ruby\",\"Ruby-on-Rails\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"MySQL\",\"PostgreSQL\",\"Elasticsearch\",\"MongoDB\",\"PowerShell\",\"Bash\",\"Agile\",\"Software development\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Join Esker as a Software Developer\\nAre you passionate about creating software that makes a real difference? At Esker, our R\\u0026D team is looking for a Software Developer to help shape the future of our software solutions. This is your chance to work on innovative projects that streamline business processes for companies worldwide.\\nAs part of our agile team, you’ll do more than write code—you’ll collaborate, innovate, and contribute to products that empower thousands of businesses. If you love building reliable, scalable solutions, solving complex problems and want to grow your skills in a supportive environment, we’d love to meet you.\\nKey Responsibilities:\\nApply attention to detail in writing clean, efficient, and maintainable code.\\nTake initiative and ownership of development tasks, ensuring timely delivery and high-quality outcomes.\\nCommunicate technical ideas effectively within the team and across stakeholders to align on solutions.\\nLeverage your technical expertise to design, analyze, and test new features that enhance our offerings.\\nParticipate in code reviews, providing constructive feedback to maintain accuracy and efficiency.\\nDocument development work to improve team understanding and productivity.\\nTroubleshoot and resolve issues, investigating root causes and creating innovative solutions.\\nCollaborate in an agile framework, sharing knowledge and fostering a psychologically safe environment for feedback and new ideas.\\nWhat You Bring:\\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Math, Engineering, or related field (or equivalent experience).\\nEssential Experience:\\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Math, Engineering, or related field (or equivalent experience).3+ years of professional experience developing software in a production environment using some of these technologies: TypeScript, JavaScript, C#, Python, Ruby, Ruby-on-Rails, HTML, and CSS.\\nExperience developing web software as part of a team.\\nHands-on experience with relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL, and NoSQL databases such as Elasticsearch or Mongo.\\nExperience using and scripting command line tools like PowerShell or Bash.\\nBonus points for UI/UX experience or familiarity with SAP.\\nSalary Range: $90,000-120,000\\nThis role requires hybrid work located in Middleton, WI.\\nThis posting will close Tuesday, October 20th at 12 PM CT.\\nEmployee Benefits\\nStudent loan repayment assistance\\nHybrid work environment, summer hours, and true work/life balance\\nPaid time off for community outreach and volunteer opportunities\\nYearly stipend for employee wellness, hobbies, or educational activities\\nDog-friendly work environment\\nCompetitive salary and benefits package\\nWho We Are\\nEstablished in 1985, Esker has grown into a leading provider of AI-driven process automation software with over 1,000 employees and 1,700 customers worldwide. Companies such as Arizona Cardinals Football Club, Whirlpool, Sony, Trek, Heineken, and many more use our cloud-based solutions to run more efficient and cost-effective business processes, improve customer and supplier relationships, increase employee productivity and morale, and enhance global visibility, scalability and compliance. Esker operates in five continents with global headquarters in Lyon, France, and two U.S. locations in Madison, WI, and Denver, CO.\\nCome as You Are\\nEsker is an equal opportunity employer that celebrates diversity and is committed to maintaining an inclusive and mutually respectful work environment. We do not discriminate against any qualified applicants on the basis of: race, color, national origin, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy, disability, medical history, military or veteran status, and any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Established in 1985, Esker is a leading provider of AI-driven process automation software with over 1,000 employees and 1,700 customers worldwide.\",\"Companies use Esker's cloud-based solutions to run more efficient and cost-effective business processes, improve customer and supplier relationships, increase employee productivity and morale, and enhance global visibility, scalability and compliance.\",\"Esker operates in five continents with global headquarters in Lyon, France, and two U.S. locations in Madison, WI, and Denver, CO.\"],\"about_role\":\"Join Esker's R\\u0026D team as a Software Developer to shape the future of our software solutions. This role involves working on innovative projects that streamline business processes for companies worldwide, contributing to products that empower thousands of businesses.\",\"annual_salary\":[\"$90,000-120,000\"],\"benefits\":[\"Student loan repayment assistance\",\"Hybrid work environment, summer hours, and true work/life balance\",\"Paid time off for community outreach and volunteer opportunities\",\"Yearly stipend for employee wellness, hobbies, or educational activities\",\"Dog-friendly work environment\",\"Competitive salary and benefits package\"],\"education_level\":[\"Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Math, Engineering, or related field (or equivalent experience)\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"Esker is an equal opportunity employer that celebrates diversity and is committed to maintaining an inclusive and mutually respectful work environment.\",\"We do not discriminate against any qualified applicants on the basis of: race, color, national origin, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy, disability, medical history, military or veteran status, and any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"3+ years of professional experience\"],\"location\":[\"Middleton, WI\"],\"requirements\":[\"Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Math, Engineering, or related field (or equivalent experience).\",\"3+ years of professional experience developing software in a production environment.\",\"Experience developing web software as part of a team.\",\"Hands-on experience with relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL.\",\"Hands-on experience with NoSQL databases such as Elasticsearch or Mongo.\",\"Experience using and scripting command line tools like PowerShell or Bash.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Apply attention to detail in writing clean, efficient, and maintainable code.\",\"Take initiative and ownership of development tasks, ensuring timely delivery and high-quality outcomes.\",\"Communicate technical ideas effectively within the team and across stakeholders to align on solutions.\",\"Leverage technical expertise to design, analyze, and test new features that enhance offerings.\",\"Participate in code reviews, providing constructive feedback to maintain accuracy and efficiency.\",\"Document development work to improve team understanding and productivity.\",\"Troubleshoot and resolve issues, investigating root causes and creating innovative solutions.\",\"Collaborate in an agile framework, sharing knowledge and fostering a psychologically safe environment for feedback and new ideas.\"],\"skills\":[\"TypeScript\",\"JavaScript\",\"C#\",\"Python\",\"Ruby\",\"Ruby-on-Rails\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"UI/UX\",\"SAP\"],\"work_type\":[\"Hybrid\"]}},{\"id\":\"c68cb840-da3e-45b5-ac48-ff84d1948df3\",\"source_id\":\"2410163847\",\"obfuscated_id\":41872174,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"SchoolsFirst Federal Credit Union\",\"job_url\":\"https://schoolsfirstfcu.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Tustin-CA/Software-Developer_JR106353-1\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-12T22:15:48.782128Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"CA, US\",\"CA, USA\",\"CA, United States\",\"California, US\",\"California, USA\",\"California, United States\",\"Tustin, CA, US\",\"Tustin, CA, USA\",\"Tustin, CA, United States\",\"Tustin, California, US\",\"Tustin, California, USA\",\"Tustin, California, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"b3dd82f1-1d7e-0b58-58df-4d8813f42a1c\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1413376557/mizenj1eykpdabenedg6.png\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":37.7,\"salary_max_value\":56.55,\"salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":37.7,\"ai_salary_max_value\":56.55,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\".NET\",\"C#\",\"VB.NET\",\"ASP.NET\",\"Visual Studio\",\"JavaScript\",\"HTML 5.0\",\"SQL Server\",\"TSQL\",\"Agile Methodology\",\"SCRUM\",\"XML\",\"Episys\",\"Repgen\",\"PowerOn\",\"Web Services\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"We’re always looking for diverse, talented, service-oriented people to join our exceptional team.\\nSoftware Developer\\nThe pay range for this position is listed below. Our pay ranges are built to allow for candidates with various levels of skill and experience to be considered, as well as for room for growth and tenure achieved in a role over time. Typical new hire salary offers fall within the minimum to midpoint of a pay range for many candidates. Any offer extended to a candidate will be based upon their unique set of knowledge, skills, education, and experience as well as internal equity.\\nPay Range:\\n$37.70 - $56.55\\nScheduled Weekly Hours:\\n40\\nWhat You’ll Be Doing\\nUnder direct supervision, modifies applications programs from detailed specifications. Codes, tests, debugs, documents, and maintains those programs.\\nDevelops, implements, and maintains low complexity application software using established credit union standards and specifications.\\nCodes new applications programs to meet desired user functionality.\\nRevises application software using tables, profiles, and other vendor supplied customization tools to reflect approved changes specified by users.\\nFollows general and credit union specific coding and development standards. Builds technical and functional documentation for new programs or changes to existing programs as required.\\nTest and debug new and existing application software to assure accuracy, integrity, interoperability, and completeness to achieve desired results.\\nAbility to adapt to multiple technologies. Remains knowledgeable of new and emerging technology by researching technical materials, attending seminars and training classes, and consulting with personnel from other industries.\\nProvides ongoing system support as required.\\n\\nAdditional Job Functions\\nPerforms other duties as assigned\\nComplies with regulatory compliance and assigned training requirements including but not limited to BSA regulations corresponding to their specific job duties. Failure to do so may result in disciplinary and other employment related actions.\\n\\nQualifications\\nHigh School Diploma or GED required\\nBachelor's Degree in a related field or equivalent years of experience required\\n1-3 years of prior relevant experience required\\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\\n.NET/C#, VB.NET, ASP.NET \\nVisual Studio \\nVisual SourceSafe and/or Team Foundation Server \\nJavaScript \\nHTML 5.0 \\nSQL Server/TSQL \\nAgile Methodology, SCRUM \\nXML \\nEpisys/Repgen/PowerOn \\nWeb Services \\nSymitar \\n\\nSchoolsFirst FCU is committed to Diverse, Equitable, and Inclusive Hiring\\n\\nAt SchoolsFirst FCU we are dedicated to building and growing a diverse, inclusive, and authentic Dream Team, so if you’re excited about a position or wanting to make a career change but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. Many skills are transferrable and you may be just the right candidate for the position, or for other roles we are working on. \\n\\nSchoolsFirst Federal Credit Union is committed to fostering, cultivating, and preserving a culture of diversity and inclusion. SchoolsFirst FCU is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, political affiliation, or genetic information.\\nThis organization participates in E-Verify.\"},{\"id\":\"78c8f2f3-3de7-4f30-87c5-219a84985418\",\"source_id\":\"2410510537\",\"obfuscated_id\":41911952,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Fortescue\",\"job_url\":\"https://careers-apply.fortescue.com/job/Perth-Software-Developer-WA/1368758266/\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-13T09:17:16.341304Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"AU\",\"AUS\",\"Australia\",\"Perth, WA, AU\",\"Perth, WA, AUS\",\"Perth, WA, Australia\",\"Perth, Western Australia, AU\",\"Perth, Western Australia, AUS\",\"Perth, Western Australia, Australia\",\"WA, AU\",\"WA, AUS\",\"WA, Australia\",\"Western Australia, AU\",\"Western Australia, AUS\",\"Western Australia, Australia\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"7dbc7462-3fe4-4812-9228-45315ff94108\",\"company_image_id\":\"r2ejk24w3dsxu6tnwzrs\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"AUD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":90000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":130000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Python\",\"JavaScript\",\"TypeScript\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"Angular\",\"Vue\",\"React\",\"AWS\",\"SQL\",\"Git\",\"GitHub\",\"Agile\",\"Object-oriented programming\",\"Full-stack development\",\"Backend APIs\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Our Opportunity\\n \\nWork Location:  Fortescue’s Perth office is located on the traditional lands of the Whadjuk people.\\n \\nRoster:  Monday to Friday\\n \\nFortescue is working towards its real zero decarbonisation goal. As a Software Developer in our Green Systems Development Team, you’ll help build the cloud-based applications that support this work.\\n \\nYou’ll develop software for integrated energy balance modelling, geospatial asset tracking, forecasting and data analysis. Your work will help teams across Energy Operations, Operations Planning, Integrated Planning, Green Power and Green Mobility make informed decisions.\\n \\nYou’ll contribute across the software development lifecycle—from understanding requirements and designing solutions through to development, testing, release and ongoing improvement. You’ll work closely with developers, Fortescue IT, internal users and external vendors to deliver practical, reliable software.Key Responsibilities\\n\\nBuild full-stack software solutions for new and evolving business needs.\\n\\nContribute to the team’s technical frameworks, design principles and ways of working.\\n\\n\\nDevelop and maintain application functionality and backend APIs.\\n\\n\\nHelp ensure solutions are secure, well-tested, robust and maintainable.\\n\\n\\nTurn user stories and requirements into technical tasks and estimates.\\n\\n\\nWork with an agile team to deliver against the development backlog.\\n\\n\\nPrepare and maintain clear technical documentation, including design decisions, specifications, release notes and support handovers.\\n\\n\\nContribute ideas and initiatives that improve our software and development practices.\\n\\nQualifications and Experience\\n\\n\\n5+ years’ experience developing custom software, including full-stack applications and backend APIs.\\n\\n\\nStrong Python skills and experience with JavaScript or TypeScript, HTML/CSS, and a modern framework such as Angular, Vue or React.\\n\\n\\nExperience with AWS, relational databases and SQL, plus Git/GitHub and agile development.\\n\\n\\nKnowledge of object-oriented programming and secure software practices.\\n\\n\\nA degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering or a related field, or equivalent experience.\\n\\n\\nExperience with AWS services, PostgreSQL, TimescaleDB, Snowflake, CI/CD, DevOps, testing, infrastructure as code, Terraform, Docker or Jira would be an advantage. \\n\\n\\nExperience with large-scale data solutions, energy or mining, AI, machine learning or optimisation, and AWS certifications is also desirable.\\n\\nAbout Us\\n \\n\\nBe part of something big. Fortescue is leading the world with our plan to decarbonise our iron ore operations, projects that harness renewable energy and the development of technology that will change our planet forever. \\nOur Commitment\\n \\n\\nFortescue celebrates individual strengths and team members are encouraged to bring their whole selves to work. Our global workforce drives and promotes an inclusive culture, both within our organisation and throughout the communities we interact with. Diverse backgrounds include First Nations Peoples, people with disabilities, LGBTQ+ community, gender, neurodiverse, cultural diversity, all age groups, and those with an intersectional or multiple diverse characteristics. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply.\\n\\n \\n\\nhttps://fortescue.com/careers \\n\\n \\n\\nInternal Candidates / Current Contractors please apply via Success Factors Careers Portal. For further information on how to apply please visit the Fortescue Hub. \\n\\n \\n\\nFortescue reserves the right to close applications early should a suitable pool of candidates be identified. Fortescue will never contact you to ask for payment of any kind, whether directly or through a third party.\"},{\"id\":\"48d944e3-06d9-4aba-8188-82b03ea8d31f\",\"source_id\":\"2415943531\",\"obfuscated_id\":42223082,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"AM Specialty\",\"job_url\":\"https://amspecialty.bamboohr.com/careers/67\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-15T17:24:28.280457Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"NY, US\",\"NY, USA\",\"NY, United States\",\"New York, NY, US\",\"New York, NY, USA\",\"New York, NY, United States\",\"New York, New York, US\",\"New York, New York, USA\",\"New York, New York, United States\",\"New York, US\",\"New York, USA\",\"New York, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"c686eb06-90da-418f-805f-395562045073\",\"company_image_id\":\"cfpftt0gawn4mb5lzsyg\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":55,\"salary_max_value\":74.5,\"salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":55,\"ai_salary_max_value\":74.5,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Software engineering\",\"Full-stack development\",\"AWS\",\"JavaScript\",\"TypeScript\",\"React\",\"Node.js\",\"RESTful APIs\",\"PostgreSQL\",\"DynamoDB\",\"Shopify\",\"CI/CD\",\"Infrastructure-as-code\",\"Terraform\",\"CloudFormation\",\"Event-driven architecture\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"We are contracting a Software Engineer to own and evolve our full technical stack. You will report directly to the VP of Engineering and have significant influence over architecture decisions, tooling, and product direction. This is a high-autonomy role for someone who wants to build something meaningful from the early stages and grow as the team scales.\\nWhat You'll Do\\nBuild and maintain our full-stack application across frontend, backend, APIs, and infrastructure\\nDesign and implement integrations with Shopify and other e-commerce platforms\\nOwn our AWS infrastructure: deployment pipelines, serverless functions, databases, event-driven architectures\\nDevelop data models and workflows that support insurance product delivery, claims processing, and merchant analytics\\nCollaborate directly with the CEO to translate business priorities into technical execution\\nImplement A/B testing frameworks, analytics instrumentation, and conversion optimization tooling\\nEstablish engineering best practices: CI/CD, code review, testing, documentation, and monitoring\\nMake architectural choices that allow the platform to scale from dozens of merchants to thousands\\nWhat We're Looking For\\n2 to 6 years of professional software engineering experience\\nStrong full-stack proficiency: you can build a clean frontend and a reliable backend\\nSolid experience with AWS services (Lambda, DynamoDB, EventBridge, S3, API Gateway, or similar)\\nProficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript and at least one modern frontend framework (React preferred)\\nExperience with Node.js and building RESTful or event-driven APIs\\nComfort working with relational and/or NoSQL databases (PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, Supabase, etc.)\\nSelf-starter mentality: you thrive with ambiguity, take ownership, and ship without waiting for a spec\\nStrong communication skills and comfort working directly with non-technical stakeholders\\nPreferred Qualifications\\nExperience with Shopify app development, Shopify APIs, or the Shopify ecosystem\\nFamiliarity with e-commerce platforms, checkout flows, or post-purchase experiences\\nBackground in insurtech, fintech, or regulated industries\\nExperience with infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, CDK, or CloudFormation)\\nPrior experience at an early-stage startup or as a founding/first engineer\\nFamiliarity with Supabase and webhook-driven architectures\\nWhat We Offer\\nCompetitive salary commensurate with experience\\nDirect access to leadership and outsized impact on product and company direction\\nHealth benefits and PTO\\nWork Authorization\\nApplicants must be authorized to work in the U.S. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"We are a company focused on building a meaningful technical stack from early stages and growing as the team scales.\"],\"about_role\":\"We are seeking a Software Engineer to own and evolve our full technical stack. This role offers significant influence over architecture, tooling, and product direction, with high autonomy for individuals who want to build from the early stages and grow with the team.\",\"annual_salary\":[\"Competitive salary commensurate with experience\"],\"benefits\":[\"Direct access to leadership and outsized impact on product and company direction\",\"Health benefits\",\"PTO\"],\"education_level\":[],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"Applicants must be authorized to work in the U.S. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"2 to 6 years of professional software engineering experience\",\"Early-stage startup experience\",\"Founding/first engineer experience\"],\"location\":[\"U.S.\"],\"requirements\":[\"2 to 6 years of professional software engineering experience.\",\"Strong full-stack proficiency, capable of building both frontend and backend components.\",\"Solid experience with AWS services such as Lambda, DynamoDB, EventBridge, S3, or API Gateway.\",\"Proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript and at least one modern frontend framework (React preferred).\",\"Experience with Node.js and building RESTful or event-driven APIs.\",\"Comfort working with relational and/or NoSQL databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, Supabase).\",\"Self-starter mentality with the ability to thrive in ambiguity, take ownership, and ship code independently.\",\"Strong communication skills and comfort working directly with non-technical stakeholders.\",\"Experience with Shopify app development, Shopify APIs, or the Shopify ecosystem.\",\"Familiarity with e-commerce platforms, checkout flows, or post-purchase experiences.\",\"Background in insurtech, fintech, or regulated industries.\",\"Experience with infrastructure-as-code tools like Terraform, CDK, or CloudFormation.\",\"Prior experience at an early-stage startup or as a founding/first engineer.\",\"Familiarity with Supabase and webhook-driven architectures.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Build and maintain the full-stack application across frontend, backend, APIs, and infrastructure.\",\"Design and implement integrations with Shopify and other e-commerce platforms.\",\"Own AWS infrastructure, including deployment pipelines, serverless functions, databases, and event-driven architectures.\",\"Develop data models and workflows for insurance product delivery, claims processing, and merchant analytics.\",\"Collaborate directly with the CEO to translate business priorities into technical execution.\",\"Implement A/B testing frameworks, analytics instrumentation, and conversion optimization tooling.\",\"Establish engineering best practices, including CI/CD, code review, testing, documentation, and monitoring.\",\"Make architectural choices to enable platform scalability from dozens to thousands of merchants.\"],\"skills\":[\"Full-stack development\",\"Frontend development\",\"Backend development\",\"API development\",\"AWS (Lambda, DynamoDB, EventBridge, S3, API Gateway)\",\"JavaScript\",\"TypeScript\",\"React\",\"Node.js\",\"RESTful APIs\",\"Event-driven architectures\",\"Database management (SQL, NoSQL)\",\"Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, CDK, CloudFormation)\",\"CI/CD\",\"Code review\",\"Testing\",\"Documentation\",\"Monitoring\",\"A/B testing\",\"Analytics instrumentation\",\"Conversion optimization\",\"Shopify app development\",\"Shopify APIs\",\"E-commerce platforms\",\"Supabase\",\"Webhook architectures\"],\"work_type\":[\"Contract\",\"Full-time\"]}},{\"id\":\"d8e93f64-31eb-41dd-a77b-451e33b6d19e\",\"source_id\":\"2416351078\",\"obfuscated_id\":42240806,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Oneida County Rural Telephone\",\"job_url\":\"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=3c6fc738-7498-4670-a3c9-0d47388d55c9\\u0026jobId=540603\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-15T20:17:33.613935Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Holland Patent, NY, US\",\"Holland Patent, NY, USA\",\"Holland Patent, NY, United States\",\"Holland Patent, New York, US\",\"Holland Patent, New York, USA\",\"Holland Patent, New York, United States\",\"NY, US\",\"NY, USA\",\"NY, United States\",\"New York, US\",\"New York, USA\",\"New York, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"f9f582f8-0343-416f-b587-6c476b826266\",\"company_image_id\":\"x9h1tqc3enwhp0iczyoo\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":32.36,\"salary_max_value\":53.37,\"salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":32.36,\"ai_salary_max_value\":53.37,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Software Development\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"Database Design\",\"Transact SQL\",\"PowerBuilder\",\"API Management\",\"System Integration\",\"Debugging\",\"Technical Documentation\",\"Code Review\",\"Visual Studio\",\"ASP.NET MVC\",\".NET Core\",\"C#\",\"JavaScript\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"SOFTWARE DEVELOPER\\n\\nDEPARTMENT: Operations - Software\\n\\nREPORTS TO: Software Engineering Manager\\n\\nDIRECT REPORTS: None\\n\\nSTATUS: Non-Exempt, Full-Time\\n\\nLOCATION: Holland Patent, NY, Hybrid Position \\n\\nPAY RANGE: $32.36 - $53.37 per hour\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nROLE OVERVIEW\\n\\nThe Software Developer is responsible for using their knowledge of programming languages to design and create new software. Some of the duties include meeting with users to determine their software needs (requirements gathering), coding and testing software to ensure performance and functionality and managing APIs between system.\\n\\nROLE CAPABILITIES\\n\\nSoftware Development \\u0026 Maintenance\\n\\n * Designs and builds software solutions based on defined requirements\\n * Maintains and improves existing software across multiple functionality areas\\n * Produces efficient code that supports expected functionality and performance\\n * Manages APIs and integrations between systems\\n * Corrects defects and implements fixes that restore expected behavior\\n\\nSoftware Collaboration\\n\\n * Collaborates with management, departments, and customers to identify requirements and specifications\\n * Translates user needs into development tasks and technical specifications\\n * Works within a team environment to align development work to shared requirements\\n * Assesses user feedback and observed issue patterns to recommend improvements\\n\\nTesting, Deployment \\u0026 Issue Resolution\\n\\n * Tests software to confirm performance and functionality\\n * Deploys programs, applications, and release updates\\n * Troubleshoots and debugs software issues across systems and integrations\\n * Identifies root causes and validates fixes before release\\n\\nCode Quality \\u0026 Documentation\\n\\n * Participates in code reviews to support code quality and consistency\\n * Refactors code to improve maintainability\\n * Develops technical documentation that supports future development work\\n * Maintains documentation aligned to system changes and improvements\\n\\nMINIMUM JOB QUALIFICATIONS: \\n\\n * Associate’s Degree in Computer Science and/or relevant working experience\\n * A strong understanding of HTML and CSS, Database Design Principles, and Transact SQL\\n * A willingness to learn and use the PowerBuilder development language to maintain current in-house systems\\n * Demonstrated ability to:\\n * Build and maintain trust-based relationships\\n * Communicate effectively using a variety of technologies and methods\\n * Adapt to changing priorities, processes, technologies, and business needs.\\n * Manage projects and priorities from planning through execution to achieve desired outcomes.\\n * Understand stakeholder needs, analyze information and data, and develop effective solutions that drive results.\\n * Valid driver’s license or ability to access transportation\\n * Ability to reach, sit, stand, walk, push, pull, lift, use fingers, grasp, feel, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions, exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects.\\n\\nPREFERRED JOB QUALIFICATIONS: \\n\\n * Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science\\n * Experience using Visual Studio to build solutions, ASP.NET MVC and .NET Core using C#, JavaScript (ES6)\\n * Experience or understanding of Source Control systems, especially GitHub\\n * Knowledge of Object-Relational Mapping frameworks, especially Entity Framework\\n\\nSCORECARD METRICS:\\n\\n * Reduce Lead-to-Billed Days to below 236.\\n * Improve Mean Time to Resolution (MTTR) to under 48 hours.\\n * Improve MACD completion to under 48 hours.\\n * Deliver automation and AI initiatives that reduce manual effort and improve operational performance.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[],\"about_role\":\"The Software Developer designs and creates new software using programming languages. Key responsibilities include gathering user requirements, coding, testing software for performance and functionality, and managing APIs between systems.\",\"annual_salary\":[\"$32.36 - $53.37 per hour\"],\"benefits\":[],\"education_level\":[\"Associate’s Degree in Computer Science\",\"Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[],\"experience_level\":[],\"location\":[\"Holland Patent, NY\"],\"requirements\":[\"Associate’s Degree in Computer Science and/or relevant working experience\",\"A strong understanding of HTML and CSS, Database Design Principles, and Transact SQL\",\"A willingness to learn and use the PowerBuilder development language to maintain current in-house systems\",\"Demonstrated ability to build and maintain trust-based relationships\",\"Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively using a variety of technologies and methods\",\"Demonstrated ability to adapt to changing priorities, processes, technologies, and business needs\",\"Demonstrated ability to manage projects and priorities from planning through execution to achieve desired outcomes\",\"Demonstrated ability to understand stakeholder needs, analyze information and data, and develop effective solutions that drive results\",\"Valid driver’s license or ability to access transportation\",\"Ability to reach, sit, stand, walk, push, pull, lift, use fingers, grasp, feel, talk, hear, and perform repetitive motions, exert up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Designs and builds software solutions based on defined requirements\",\"Maintains and improves existing software across multiple functionality areas\",\"Produces efficient code that supports expected functionality and performance\",\"Manages APIs and integrations between systems\",\"Corrects defects and implements fixes that restore expected behavior\",\"Collaborates with management, departments, and customers to identify requirements and specifications\",\"Translates user needs into development tasks and technical specifications\",\"Works within a team environment to align development work to shared requirements\",\"Assesses user feedback and observed issue patterns to recommend improvements\",\"Tests software to confirm performance and functionality\",\"Deploys programs, applications, and release updates\",\"Troubleshoots and debugs software issues across systems and integrations\",\"Identifies root causes and validates fixes before release\",\"Participates in code reviews to support code quality and consistency\",\"Refactors code to improve maintainability\",\"Develops technical documentation that supports future development work\",\"Maintains documentation aligned to system changes and improvements\"],\"skills\":[\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"Database Design Principles\",\"Transact SQL\",\"PowerBuilder\",\"Visual Studio\",\"ASP.NET MVC\",\".NET Core\",\"C#\",\"JavaScript (ES6)\",\"Source Control systems\",\"GitHub\",\"Object-Relational Mapping frameworks\",\"Entity Framework\"],\"work_type\":[\"Hybrid\",\"Full-Time\"]}},{\"id\":\"b13bb042-bcbc-4d2a-9e44-4075da799686\",\"source_id\":\"2416943323\",\"obfuscated_id\":42281929,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"TEKsystems\",\"job_url\":\"https://careers.teksystems.com/us/en/job/JP-006337160/Software-Developer\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-16T02:16:07.287557Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Irving, TX, US\",\"Irving, TX, USA\",\"Irving, TX, United States\",\"Irving, Texas, US\",\"Irving, Texas, USA\",\"Irving, Texas, United States\",\"TX, US\",\"TX, USA\",\"TX, United States\",\"Texas, US\",\"Texas, USA\",\"Texas, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"10dccb4a-b6e0-239f-ce61-cf9f549e1ad4\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1428737538/yn0fchgqpwt2nnb17yhy.png\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":65,\"salary_max_value\":73,\"salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":65,\"ai_salary_max_value\":73,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Servicenow\",\"Itsm\",\"Discovery\",\"Certificate Management\",\"Inbound Integrations\",\"Staging Tables\",\"Transforms\",\"Identification And Reconciliation Engine\",\"Ire\",\"Cad Certification\",\"Csa Certification\",\"Incident Management\",\"Software Development\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Service Now Developer\\nLocation 3x onsite in Charlotte, NC or Irving, TX\\nMust be able to work W2 : Cannot Provide Sponsorship!\\nDescription\\nThese roles will involve working on discovery, integrations, and incident management within the ServiceNow platform. The developers will be matrixed into the client's project and will report to the Senior Manager of IT Service Management. There is an effort to enhance the end-to-end certificate management process, which includes discovery, integrations, and incident-related tasks. \\nContribute to the enhancement of the certificate management process, focusing on discovery and integrations.\\nHandle inbound integrations into ServiceNow, including setting up staging tables, transforms, and Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE) rules.1\\nAssist with incident-related tasks within the certificate management scope.\\nSkills\\nservicenow, itsm, discovery, \\nMust have CDA \\u0026 CSA Certificates \\nTop Skills Details\\nservicenow,itsm,discovery\\nAdditional Skills \\u0026 Qualifications\\nServiceNow Certificate Management Module: Experience using this module is highly desired. \\nServiceNow Discovery: This is a big one, and even if a candidate lacks certificate management experience, strong discovery experience is crucial. \\nInbound Integrations into ServiceNow: Candidates must have experience with inbound integrations. \\nCAD and CSA Certifications: Required, with a preference for those certified for at least five months. \\nServiceNow Configuration: Candidates should know how to set up staging tables, transforms, and IREs (Identification and Reconciliation Engine). \\nProject Context \\u0026 Impact: \\nThe roles are for an effort to \\\"beef up the certificate management process end to end,\\\" including discovery and integrations. This highlights the importance and impact of the work. \\nThe team is deploying new AI functionality every month in the ITSM space, with more coming in 2027, indicating a forward-thinking and evolving environment. \\nWhat to Emphasize to Candidates: \\nThe opportunity to work on critical, impactful projects that are enhancing core IT service management processes. \\nThe chance to work in a dynamic environment with continuous deployment of new AI functionality.\\nExperience Level\\nExpert Level\\nJob Type \\u0026 Location\\nThis is a Contract position based out of Irving, TX.\\nPay and Benefits\\nThe pay range for this position is $65.00 - $73.00/hr. \\nIndividual compensation offered for this position within this range will depend on many factors, including qualifications, skills, relevant experience, job knowledge, geographic location, internal equity, and other pertinent job-related factors.\\nEligibility requirements apply to some benefits and may depend on your job classification and length of employment. Benefits are subject to change and may be subject to specific elections, plan, or program terms. If eligible, the benefits available for this temporary role may include the following: Medical, dental \\u0026 vision Critical Illness, Accident, and Hospital 401(k) Retirement Plan Pre-tax and Roth post-tax contributions available Life Insurance (Voluntary Life \\u0026 AD\\u0026D for the employee and dependents) Short and long-term disability Health Spending Account (HSA) Transportation benefits Employee Assistance Program Time Off/Leave (PTO, Vacation or Sick Leave)\\nWorkplace Type\\nThis is a hybrid position in Irving,TX.\\nApplication Deadline\\nThis position is anticipated to close on Oct 22, 2026.\\nAbout TEKsystems\\nWe're partners in transformation. We help clients activate ideas and solutions to take advantage of a new world of opportunity. We are a team of 80,000 strong, working with over 6,000 clients, including 80% of the Fortune 500, across North America, Europe and Asia. As an industry leader in Full-Stack Technology Services, Talent Services, and real-world application, we work with progressive leaders to drive change. That's the power of true partnership. TEKsystems is an Allegis Group company. \\nThe company is an equal opportunity employer and will consider all applications without regards to race, sex, age, color, religion, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information or any characteristic protected by law.\\nAbout TEKsystems and TEKsystems Global Services \\nWere a leading provider of business and technology services. We accelerate business transformation for our customers. Our expertise in strategy, design, execution and operations unlocks business value through a range of solutions. Were a team of 80,000 strong, working with over 6,000 customers, including 80% of the Fortune 500 across North America, Europe and Asia, who partner with us for our scale, full-stack capabilities and speed. Were strategic thinkers, hands-on collaborators, helping customers capitalize on change and master the momentum of technology. Were building tomorrow by delivering business outcomes and making positive impacts in our global communities. TEKsystems and TEKsystems Global Services are Allegis Group companies. Learn more at TEKsystems.com.\\nThe company is an equal opportunity employer and will consider all applications without regard to race, sex, age, color, religion, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information or any characteristic protected by law.\\nSan Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance: Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, for all positions located in the city and county of San Francisco, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\\nMassachusetts Lie Detector: It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.\\nUse of Artificial Intelligence (AI): We may use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to support parts of our hiring process, including sourcing, screening, and evaluating candidates. AI helps assess applications and qualifications, but final decisions are made by our hiring team. By applying, you acknowledge and agree that your application may be reviewed using AI tools.\"},{\"id\":\"06b2ebf7-a79a-4c1e-8b38-ecd9e0d31d24\",\"source_id\":\"2414630710\",\"obfuscated_id\":42154528,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"ASM\",\"job_url\":\"https://jobs.workable.com/view/gottgQ3ufEkw8PtASvG3qX/hybrid-software-developer-in-temecula-at-asm\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-15T01:16:11.665548Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"CA, US\",\"CA, USA\",\"CA, United States\",\"California, US\",\"California, USA\",\"California, United States\",\"Temecula, CA, US\",\"Temecula, CA, USA\",\"Temecula, CA, United States\",\"Temecula, California, US\",\"Temecula, California, USA\",\"Temecula, California, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"519d4360-2b88-e036-a9a9-9dfdc25a8172\",\"company_image_id\":\"ocuxshah6ep1aedyd4pm\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":85000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":130000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"ASP.NET\",\"Javascript\",\"SQL\",\"React JS\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"C#\",\"MS SQL\",\"GitHub\",\"Version control\",\"Cloud web-services\",\"Azure\",\"TeamCity\",\"CI integrations\",\"API development\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Note: We are working hybrid with at least 2 days per week in the office (Temecula, CA). During onboarding you will likely need to be 3-4 days per week.\\nAt ASM we build best-in-class products for health care administration and quality assurance. We use the latest technology to provide products to over 1,200 health care organizations worldwide. Founded in 1982 we have developed a great team to build great products.\\nWhat would I do at ASM?\\nWith thousands of hospitals across the world, you would help develop new features, new products, design \\u0026 re-design UIs, and help maintain existing services and products offered by ASM. You will need to rely on an understanding of ASP.NET, Javascript, and SQL to craft changes that have an impact. \\nWho is the ideal candidate? \\nYou understand the importance of user experience, quality, and reliability. You empathize with the struggles of end-users and advocate on their behalf. You get excited solving design and performance challenges with other developers, building reusable components, and then continuing to improve those services and components.\\nResponsibilities:\\nImprove and maintain our React and ASP.NET Components\\nConnect our front-end components to the API and databases\\nWork on cloud web-services that power the products\\nDesign and maintain components for our web and mobile products\\nConceptualize original ideas that bring simplicity and user friendliness to complex ideas\\nProficiency in HTML, CSS, and Javascript\\nFamiliarity with C# (or similar)\\nFamiliarity with MS SQL (or similar)\\nFamiliarity with React JS (or similar)\\nFamiliarity with GitHub and version control\\nTo care deeply about reliability and performance\\nA strong attention to detail\\nBonus experience:\\nFamiliarity with iOS and/or Android\\nFamiliarity with ASP.NET\\nFamiliarity with Azure\\nFamiliarity with TeamCity and CI integrations\\nFamiliarity with user-facing APIs\\nHealthcare Experience\\nWe offer everything you'd expect from a successful and established software company.\\n401(k) retirement plan with employer match.\\nEvery developer and designer has an SSD-enabled laptop, dual 24\\\" LED monitors, Sit/Stand Desks, Herman-Miller chairs.\\nModern Technology - We stay up-to-date with the latest in our diverse technology stack.\\nCatered lunches on Wednesdays\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Founded in 1982, ASM builds best-in-class products for healthcare administration and quality assurance using the latest technology.\",\"We serve over 1,200 healthcare organizations worldwide.\",\"We have developed a great team to build great products.\"],\"about_role\":\"At ASM, we build best-in-class products for healthcare administration and quality assurance, serving over 1,200 healthcare organizations worldwide. You will help develop new features, new products, design and re-design UIs, and maintain existing services and products. This role requires an understanding of ASP.NET, Javascript, and SQL to craft impactful changes.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[\"401(k) retirement plan with employer match\",\"SSD-enabled laptop, dual 24\\\" LED monitors, Sit/Stand Desks, Herman-Miller chairs\",\"Modern Technology\",\"Catered lunches on Wednesdays\"],\"education_level\":[],\"equal_opportunity\":[],\"experience_level\":[\"Mid-level\"],\"location\":[\"Temecula, CA\"],\"requirements\":[\"Proficiency in HTML, CSS, and Javascript\",\"Familiarity with C# (or similar)\",\"Familiarity with MS SQL (or similar)\",\"Familiarity with React JS (or similar)\",\"Familiarity with GitHub and version control\",\"Care deeply about reliability and performance\",\"A strong attention to detail\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Improve and maintain React and ASP.NET Components\",\"Connect front-end components to the API and databases\",\"Work on cloud web-services that power the products\",\"Design and maintain components for web and mobile products\",\"Conceptualize original ideas that bring simplicity and user friendliness to complex ideas\"],\"skills\":[\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"Javascript\",\"C#\",\"MS SQL\",\"React JS\",\"GitHub\",\"ASP.NET\",\"Azure\",\"TeamCity\",\"CI integrations\",\"User-facing APIs\",\"iOS\",\"Android\"],\"work_type\":[\"Hybrid\"]}},{\"id\":\"32438525-c6af-4088-b879-bdac02e80f53\",\"source_id\":\"2418289371\",\"obfuscated_id\":42342199,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Kongsberg Geospatial Ltd\",\"job_url\":\"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=8fd13316-1f93-4d98-b39c-59a884b85873\\u0026jobId=597437\\u0026ccId=9201247417322_3\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-16T18:17:27.720635Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"CA\",\"CAN\",\"Canada\",\"ON, CA\",\"ON, CAN\",\"ON, Canada\",\"Ontario, CA\",\"Ontario, CAN\",\"Ontario, Canada\",\"Ottawa, ON, CA\",\"Ottawa, ON, CAN\",\"Ottawa, ON, Canada\",\"Ottawa, Ontario, CA\",\"Ottawa, Ontario, CAN\",\"Ottawa, Ontario, Canada\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"e3e1bf7f-c65d-468d-af48-9d3645e05f7b\",\"company_image_id\":\"asctqzhlhhxlpwta30ak\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"CAD\",\"salary_min_value\":75000,\"salary_max_value\":125000,\"salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"CAD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":125000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Modern C++\",\"Software Development\",\"Backend Systems\",\"Software Libraries\",\"Platform Development\",\"Object-Oriented Design\",\"API Design\",\"Linux\",\"Windows\",\"Git\",\"Agile Development\",\"Performance Optimization\",\"Debugging\",\"Code Reviews\",\"Vulkan\",\"Geospatial Systems\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"About Kongsberg Geospatial\\n\\nKongsberg Geospatial does challenging work that matters. We are an industry leading software company that has been delivering real-time geospatial technology solutions for Defence and Aerospace applications worldwide for over 30 years. \\n\\nSince 2006, we have been a wholly owned subsidiary of Kongsberg Defence \\u0026 Aerospace in Norway and we are an integral part of many key programs there. Externally, our technology is relied upon and trusted for a wide range of applications including air defense, search and rescue, drone delivery systems, and autonomous vehicle tracking. Our team members make a real impact in people's lives\\n\\nWhat we’re looking for\\n\\nAre you a software professional that enjoys creating robust, well‑designed solutions that other developers love to build on? Do you thrive on solving problems at a systems or platform level? Do you enjoy working in small teams and having influence on architecture and design? If so, this role may be for you!\\n\\nOur team is growing and we’re looking for a C++ Software Developer to contribute to a software platform and SDKs that rapidly process and analyze geospatial data.\\n\\nThis is a hybrid position working out of our Ottawa, Ontario office. \\n\\nThis position may require travel within and outside of Canada approximately twice a year.\\n\\nDuties include\\n\\n * Work with a small team to analyse, design, build, test, and document software libraries to function across multiple platforms.\\n\\n * Develop and maintain high-performance software using C++.\\n * Emphasize modular, decoupled, and composable design to support long‑term evolution.\\n * Optimize existing code for performance, reliability, and maintainability.\\n * Debug and troubleshoot issues in complex systems.\\n * Conduct code reviews and ensure adherence to coding standards.\\n * Incorporate feedback from end users as well as members of the project team to solve any design or usability issues.\\n * Participate in Agile/Scrum development processes, including sprint planning and retrospective.\\n\\nYou Have\\n\\n * A Canadian security clearance or eligibility to obtain one. \\n * A post-secondary degree in a field related to Computer Science or Engineering or equivalent relevant experience. \\n * Minimum 4 years experience in Software Development (with a strong focus on C++).\\n * A problem‑solving mindset. You are motivated to think beyond immediate requirements and design flexible solutions.\\n * Ability to adapt quickly to changes in technology and scope of work. \\n * Strong verbal, written and presentation skills, with the ability to effectively communicate technical concepts to internal and external stakeholders.\\n * Strong planning and organizational skills.\\n * Ability to work both independently and as part of a team.\\n\\nExperience in the following areas: \\n\\n * Strong development experience in modern C++.\\n * Designing and implementing backend systems, libraries, or shared platforms.\\n * Applying object‑oriented design principles and interface‑driven development.\\n * Developing on Linux and/or Windows using common toolchains (e.g., Visual Studio, GCC, Clang).\\n * Managing software configurations with Git or similar version control systems. \\n * Agile development processes. \\n\\nIt will be great if you have … \\n\\nExperience in some of the following areas depending on the project and role: \\n\\n * Experience with Vulkan or GPU compute programming.\\n * Experience with other programming languages or technologies (e.g., QT, Python, Go) and cross‑language interoperability.\\n * Experience designing APIs or frameworks intended for consumption by other developers.\\n * Experience and domain knowledge of geospatial, sensor, or tracking systems.\\n * Experience and domain knowledge with one or more of Defence, ATC, and UAV applications and operations.\\n\\nThe base salary range for this role is $75,000 - $125,000. Individual pay is determined by a number of factors including job-related skills, experience, internal equity and relevant education or training.\\n\\nHow to Apply:\\n\\nVisit our website www.kongsberggeospatial.com [http://www.kongsberggeospatial.com] to learn more about us. If you fulfill the requirements and skills listed above, we look forward to hearing from you. \\n\\nAccommodations are available upon request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process. If you require accommodation, please notify us in the application process.\\n\\nDue to the volume of applicants, only those selected for an interview will be contacted. We appreciate your interest in Kongsberg Geospatial.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\"}],\"total_items\":400,\"total_pages\":34},\"message\":\"success\"}"
