          "cookies": [],
          "content": {
            "size": 99323,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"data\":{\"jobs\":[{\"id\":\"d15c33f3-4ec6-4c96-a529-b6b9cabc2f39\",\"source_id\":\"2418658820\",\"obfuscated_id\":42378909,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"ASRC Federal\",\"job_url\":\"https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/asrcfh/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/30171\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-16T22:18:47.055544Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"OK, US\",\"OK, USA\",\"OK, United States\",\"Oklahoma City, OK, US\",\"Oklahoma City, OK, USA\",\"Oklahoma City, OK, United States\",\"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, US\",\"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, USA\",\"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States\",\"Oklahoma, US\",\"Oklahoma, USA\",\"Oklahoma, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"36c76bfd-01a8-1eb1-3094-0c2fc04c77ae\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1471597273/mfzgkqywwi2srkswf6x0.jpg\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":110000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"C\",\"C++\",\"Python\",\"Git\",\"VLANs\",\"VPNs\",\"NAT\",\"ACLs\",\"Network monitoring\",\"OSI model\",\"TCP/IP\",\"Subnetting\",\"Routing\",\"Switching\",\"LabVIEW\",\"SQL\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"ASRC Federal is a leading government contractor furthering missions in space, public health and defense. As an Alaska Native owned corporation, our work helps secure an enduring future for our shareholders. Join our team and discover why we are a top veteran employer and Certified Great Place to Work™\\n​​ASRC Federal Advanced Research LLC (AFAR)​ is seeking a ​Software Developer​ to join our ​Communications Remote Maintenance \\u0026 Monitoring (CRMM)​ team that supports the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA). This is a ​full-time​ ​on-site​ position at the ​Mike Monroney Aeronautical Center (MMAC)​ in ​Oklahoma City, OK​. \\n​​The FAA's Communications Remote Maintenance and Monitoring (CRMM) system—specifically supported by technologies like the multi-protocol communications remote monitoring panel—enables secure, continuous remote oversight of National Airspace System (NAS) communication networks.​ \\nCitizenship/Permanent Residency Requirement \\nAll candidates must have the following to pass the Federal Background Investigation and obtain the FAA Public Trust security clearance. \\nBe a US Citizen. \\nHas resided in the US for three (3) consecutive years.\\nRealID Driver’s License/ID or current US Passport. \\nRelocation Requirement \\nCandidate must reside or be willing to relocate within a commutable distance to the ​Mike Monroney Aeronautical Center (MMAC)​ in ​Oklahoma City, OK​. \\nEducation \\u0026 Experience Requirement \\nAll non-US Degrees must have a US Equivalency Certificate provided by the candidate at the time of application. \\nA ​Bachelors​ degree in ​Computer Science or related IT fields, with a minimum of thirty (30) semester hours in a combination of mathematics, statistics, and computer science may be substituted in lieu of the computer science degree, depending on other qualifications and experience.\\nExperience with NAS facilities, systems, and equipment is ​desired​.\\n​​0 - 3​ years of related work experience. \\nRequired Skills \\nProficient in programming languages and scripts used in model and tool development (C, C++, Python).\\nFamiliarity with hardware system design, schematics, and interconnects.\\nExperience with source control systems such as Git.\\nKnowledge of VLANs, VPNs, NAT, ACLs, and network segmentation.\\nSkilled in network monitoring and diagnostic tools.\\nStrong understanding of the OSI model, TCP/IP communications, subnetting, routing, and switching.\\nSupport tasks in lab, field, and production environments under senior engineer guidance.​ \\nAbility to: \\nWork independently, as well as on a team, in an agile environment. \\nResearch, troubleshoot and problem solve quickly. \\nLearn on the job/willing to self-teach. \\nCommunicate effectively through verbal and written communication with high organization.\\nWrite clear, structured technical documentation and explain complex technical issues to non-technical personnel.\\nPreferred Skills \\nAbility to take and support field service calls.\\nProvide real-time troubleshooting support to field technicians.\\nDocument incident findings and corrective actions.\\nSupport remote and on-site system diagnostics.\\nParticipate in after-hours or mission-critical support when required.\\nProvide software development support for configuring devices and hardware.\\nConfigure and maintain network hardware including routers and switches from various vendors​. \\nEssential Daily Job Duties \\nPerform research and maintenance of software systems.\\nOriginate, write, test, update, and document projects supporting system software.\\nLead coordination, drafting, reviewing, and editing of technical reports and drawings for final approval and distribution.\\nDevelop plans and techniques to address real-time and anticipated problems, including integration of new products and code review issues.\\nProvide support for modernization and enhancement of systems as requested by the government.\\nIdentify needs and drive development and implementation of major processes.\\nHandle and document trouble calls from system product end users.\\nProvide support using LabVIEW, C, C++, SQL, and Python (2 and 3).​ \\nWork Environment \\nStandard flexible work schedule. \\nTravel is ​10 - 25%​.\\nCubicle environment. \\nWe invest in the lives of our employees, both in and out of the workplace, by providing competitive pay and benefits packages. Benefits offered may include health care, dental, vision, life insurance; 401(k); education assistance; paid time off including PTO, holidays, and any other paid leave required by law. The salary offered will depend on several factors including, but not limited to, relevant experience, skills, education, geographic location, internal equity, business needs, and other factors permitted by law. Posted pay ranges are a general guideline only and are not a guarantee of compensation or salary.\\n\\nEEO Statement\\nASRC Federal and its Subsidiaries are Equal Opportunity employers. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, gender, color, age, sexual orientation, gender identification, national origin, religion, marital status, ancestry, citizenship, disability, protected veteran status, or any other factor prohibited by applicable law.\"},{\"id\":\"1bea8129-e724-42d2-91bf-463b3514c269\",\"source_id\":\"2421598541\",\"obfuscated_id\":42523082,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"ASSA ABLOY\",\"job_url\":\"https://assaabloy.jobs2web.com/job/Halmstad-Software-Developer-302-41/1448993233/\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-19T14:15:45.259805Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"HA, SE\",\"HA, SWE\",\"HA, Sweden\",\"Halland, SE\",\"Halland, SWE\",\"Halland, Sweden\",\"Halmstad, HA, SE\",\"Halmstad, HA, SWE\",\"Halmstad, HA, Sweden\",\"Halmstad, Halland, SE\",\"Halmstad, Halland, SWE\",\"Halmstad, Halland, Sweden\",\"SE\",\"SWE\",\"Sweden\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"1e7b570a-930e-be3a-9288-13bbd7c392f9\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1487407585/yvnaglgo3zmctvp4pmne.png\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"SEK\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":400000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":600000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\".NET\",\"C#\",\".NET MAUI\",\"Kotlin\",\"Swift\",\"Azure\",\"CI/CD\",\"Software testing\",\"System architecture\",\"Agile\",\"Scrum\",\"Git\",\"Jira\",\"Confluence\",\"Python\",\"Unit testing\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Är du redo för en spännande utmaning? Intelligent Care AB, en del av Care Technologies inom ASSA ABLOY, söker en engagerad App utvecklare!\\nBli en del av vårt team i Halmstad och upplev en samarbetskultur där du får möjlighet att bygga en karriär att vara stolt över.\\nPå ASSA ABLOY IntelligentCare utvecklar vi teknik som gör verklig skillnad inom vård och omsorg. Som en del av ASSA ABLOY Care Technologies bygger vi nästa generations plattformar för digital access, larmhantering och datadrivna tjänster.\\nEfter årsskiftet flyttar vi in i helt nya, moderna lokaler i Halmstad, som även blir nordisk hubb för produktion och logistik inom Care Technologies. Rollen är placerad i Halmstad, men vi arbetar hybrid och kombinerar kontorsarbete, nära teamsamarbete och distansarbete utifrån verksamhetens behov.\\n \\nVad du kommer att göra som vår App utvecklare\\nSom Apputvecklare hos ASSA ABLOY Care Technologies blir du en viktig del av vårt utvecklingsteam på IntelligentCare i Halmstad. Tillsammans med teamet utvecklar, testar och förvaltar du appar och mjukvarulösningar som gör vardagen enklare och tryggare inom äldreomsorgen. Du arbetar nära Product Owner och Solutions Architect och bidrar till att våra produkter håller hög kvalitet, är tekniskt framtidssäkra och levereras i tid.\\nDu blir en del av ett tvärfunktionellt utvecklingsteam där apputveckling sker i nära samarbete med UX, QA och backendutvecklare. Tillsammans tar ni ansvar för hela utvecklingsprocessen, från idé och design till färdig lösning, leverans och förvaltning.\\nI denna roll rapporterar man till Team Manager Development.\\n \\nAnsvarsområden som App utvecklare\\n\\nUtveckla nya appar och tjänster i vår molnmiljö samt vidareutveckla och förbättra befintliga lösningar.\\nSäkerställa hög kvalitet genom unit- och integrationstester, regelbunden buggfixning och refaktorering samt att koden följer våra standarder för kodning, integritet och säkerhet.\\nDelta i kravarbetet och bidra med feedback i design- och kodgranskningar, så att det alltid finns en tydlig definition of done.\\nDokumentera kod och arbetssätt, presentera ditt arbete för teamet och andra delar av organisationen samt ansvara för tilldelade informationssäkerhetsfrågor.\\nLösa mer avancerade supportärenden (3rd line) och stötta vid integrationer i samarbete med produktorganisationen, supporten och externa partners.\\n\\n \\nFärdigheterna och erfarenheten du behöver:\\n\\nKandidatexamen inom datavetenskap eller motsvarande praktisk erfarenhet, samt minst 3 års erfarenhet av mjukvaruutveckling.\\nGedigen erfarenhet av .NET och C#.\\nErfarenhet av apputveckling, helst med .NET MAUI, alternativt Kotlin eller Swift.\\nErfarenhet av Azure, CI/CD och pipelines, mjukvarutestning samt gärna systemarkitektur.\\nVan att arbeta agilt enligt Scrum med verktyg som Git, Jira och Confluence; kunskap i skriptspråk som Python är meriterande.\\n\\n \\nDu brinner för mjukvaruutveckling och ser kvalitet som något hela teamet tar ansvar för, inte bara en del av jobbet. Du är nyfiken, självgående och har ett stort intresse för ny teknik, testautomatisering och pipelines. Du är också intresserad av hur AI-verktyg kan användas i utvecklingsarbetet. Hos oss på ASSA ABLOY har vi flera communities för GenAI som vi uppmuntrar alla våra utvecklare att vara en aktiv del av.\\nSom person är du positiv och driven, och du trivs i ett team där man både delar med sig av sin kunskap och gärna lär sig nya saker av andra. Du vill skapa verkligt värde för våra kunder och användare, och du tar gärna initiativ för att förbättra både våra produkter och vårt sätt att arbeta. Eftersom vi arbetar på plats på kontoret minst tre dagar i veckan är det viktigt att du kan vara på plats när arbetet kräver det. Du uttrycker dig obehindrat i svenska och engelska, både i tal och skrift.\\n \\nVad vi erbjuder\\n\\nMöjlighet att påverka produkter och lösningar som förbättrar människors vardag och gör skillnad för samhället.\\nEn innovativ utvecklingsmiljö med moderna tekniker inom .NET, Azure, CI/CD och AI.\\nKompetensutveckling och internationella karriärmöjligheter inom ASSA ABLOY.\\nKonkurrenskraftiga villkor och förmåner.\\n\\n \\nVi granskar ansökningar regelbundet, så vänta inte\\nVi bygger mångsidiga och inkluderande team och uppmuntrar alla som kan se sig själva motiverade att arbeta mot omsorgsaktörer med vårt produktsortiment att söka. Skapa bara din profil och ansök här.\\nFör att säkerställa att din personliga information är trygg hanterar vi inga ansökningar via e-post eller post. Vid frågor om tjänsten eller rekryteringsprocessen, kontakta gärna Khalil Kabakibi, Talent Acquisition Business Partner, på khalil.kabakibi@assaabloy.com\\nBeroende på rollens riskprofil kan en bakgrundskontroll behöva genomföras. Slutkandidater kan därför bli föremål för en bakgrundskontroll. Genomförandet av bakgrundskontrollen kräver samtycke och baseras på vår integritetspolicy för sökande.\\nVill du veta mer om oss? Besök www.assaabloy.com We are the ASSA ABLOY GroupOur people have made us the global leader in access solutions. In return, we open doors for them wherever they go. With nearly 63,000 colleagues in more than 70 different countries, we help billions of people experience a more open world. Our innovations make all sorts of spaces – physical and virtual – safer, more secure, and easier to access. \\nAs an employer, we value results – not titles, or backgrounds. We empower our people to build their career around their aspirations and our ambitions – supporting them with regular feedback, training, and development opportunities. Our colleagues think broadly about where they can make the most impact, and we encourage them to grow their role locally, regionally, or even internationally.\\nAs we welcome new people on board, it’s important to us to have diverse, inclusive teams, and we value different perspectives and experiences.\\n#LI-WGIE\"},{\"id\":\"ad400864-4368-4e62-a138-39b9a6d873ec\",\"source_id\":\"2418182849\",\"obfuscated_id\":42336376,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Leidos\",\"job_url\":\"https://leidos.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Eagan-MN/Software-Developer_R-00186494-1\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-16T17:21:03.305408Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Ashburn, VA, US\",\"Ashburn, VA, USA\",\"Ashburn, VA, United States\",\"Ashburn, Virginia, US\",\"Ashburn, Virginia, USA\",\"Ashburn, Virginia, United States\",\"Eagan, MN, US\",\"Eagan, MN, USA\",\"Eagan, MN, United States\",\"Eagan, Minnesota, US\",\"Eagan, Minnesota, USA\",\"Eagan, Minnesota, United States\",\"Gaithersburg, MD, US\",\"Gaithersburg, MD, USA\",\"Gaithersburg, MD, United States\",\"Gaithersburg, Maryland, US\",\"Gaithersburg, Maryland, USA\",\"Gaithersburg, Maryland, United States\",\"MD, US\",\"MD, USA\",\"MD, United States\",\"MN, US\",\"MN, USA\",\"MN, United States\",\"Maryland, US\",\"Maryland, USA\",\"Maryland, United States\",\"Minnesota, US\",\"Minnesota, USA\",\"Minnesota, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\",\"VA, US\",\"VA, USA\",\"VA, United States\",\"Virginia, US\",\"Virginia, USA\",\"Virginia, United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"504f4b06-6124-a0c9-1925-2cdef5afab6f\",\"company_image_id\":\"u34x2the1lwhp4vwiuwt\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":69550,\"salary_max_value\":125725,\"salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":69550,\"ai_salary_max_value\":125725,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Java\",\"React\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"JavaScript\",\"Linux\",\"Git\",\"Subversion\",\"Unit Testing\",\"Cloud-Based Systems\",\"Agile\",\"SAFe\",\"RESTful APIs\",\"Spring Boot\",\"Python\",\"DevSecOps\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Leidos is seeking Software Developers to join the Air Traffic Business Area within the Homeland Sector, supporting the development of next-generation flight service and air traffic systems. This work aligns with the FAA’s broader initiative to modernize legacy flight service capabilities, replacing aging infrastructure with scalable, cloud-based platforms designed to improve safety and operational efficiency—particularly in remote and high-dependency aviation environments. These efforts focus on delivering mission-critical, future-ready solutions that provide safety-critical flight services to the pilot community.\\n\\n\\nAs a member of a Scaled Agile software development organization, you will contribute to the technical execution of a program that integrates proven, globally deployed technologies with modern cloud-native capabilities. You will work alongside cross-functional teams and technical leaders to deliver predictable outcomes in a highly regulated, safety-critical environment. \\n\\nIn this position, you will design and implement software solutions independently while working closely with systems engineering, product delivery, and DevSecOps teams. The primary focus is on developing containerized applications within an Agile/SAFe environment. This position supports government programs and requires the ability to obtain and maintain a favorable Public Trust investigation.\\n\\nPrimary Responsibilities:\\n\\nResponsible for software development activities both individually and as a member of a team including writing, testing, debugging, and maintaining source code within an Agile environment.\\nActively participate in daily stand-ups, Release Planning, and other related team activities.\\nWrite and execute unit and functional tests.\\nTroubleshoot and participate in the resolution of technical issues in lab and operational environments.\\nProvide support as needed for system engineering, test engineering, and system owner teams.\\n\\nBasic Qualifications\\nBachelor’s degree in computer science or a related field with 2-4 years of relevant experience or a Master’s degree with less than 2 years of experience. \\nExperience with Java programming language\\nExperience with React\\nExperience with Web development and commonly used front-end tools and languages (HTML, CSS, JavaScript)\\nExperience with Linux\\nExperience with version control systems such as Git or Subversion\\nExperience with common development tools and IDEs (Eclipse, VS Code, etc.)\\nKnowledge of AI-assisted software development tools and workflows (i.e. Claude Code, Codex, etc.)\\nKnowledge of Cloud-based systems\\nKnowledge of unit testing tools such as Junit and Mockito\\nUnderstanding of sound software development principles and practices\\nAbility to plan and prioritize personal tasking and be able to communicate effectively verbally and in writing\\nIndependent thinker, capable of performing high quality work, both independently and with a team in a fast-moving environment\\nAbility to obtain SF-85 Public Trust suitability determination\\nUS citizenship required\\n\\n\\nPreferred Qualifications\\nKnowledge of or experience working within the Agile/SAFe framework\\nKnowledge of or experience with RESTful API, JSON, XML, XSD\\nKnowledge of or experience with Spring Framework, Spring Security, and Spring Boot\\nKnowledge of or experience with Python programming language\\nKnowledge of or experience with Ansible playbooks and YAML\\nKnowledge of or experience with Linux shell scripting\\nKnowledge of DevSecOps practices and CI/CD pipelines\\nKnowledge of or experience with MongoDB\\nKnowledge of air traffic control and flight services\\n\\nATMC\\nIf you're looking for comfort, keep scrolling. At Leidos, we outthink, outbuild, and outpace the status quo — because the mission demands it. We're not hiring followers. We're recruiting the ones who disrupt, provoke, and refuse to fail. Step 10 is ancient history. We're already at step 30 — and moving faster than anyone else dares.\\nOriginal Posting:\\nJune 30, 2026\\nFor U.S. Positions: While subject to change based on business needs, Leidos reasonably anticipates that this job requisition will remain open for at least 3 days with an anticipated close date of no earlier than 3 days after the original posting date as listed above.\\nPay Range:\\nPay Range $69,550.00 - $125,725.00\\nThe Leidos pay range for this job level is a general guideline only and not a guarantee of compensation or salary. Additional factors considered in extending an offer include (but are not limited to) responsibilities of the job, education, experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as internal equity, alignment with market data, applicable bargaining agreement (if any), or other law.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Leidos outthinks, outbuilds, and outpaces the status quo.\",\"They are not hiring followers, but individuals who disrupt, provoke, and refuse to fail.\"],\"about_role\":\"Leidos is seeking Software Developers to support the development of next-generation flight service and air traffic systems. This role involves contributing to the modernization of legacy flight service capabilities by developing scalable, cloud-based platforms to enhance safety and operational efficiency. The position focuses on delivering mission-critical, future-ready solutions for safety-critical flight services.\",\"annual_salary\":[\"$69,550.00 - $125,725.00\"],\"benefits\":[],\"education_level\":[\"Bachelor's degree in computer science or a related field\",\"Master's degree\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[],\"experience_level\":[\"2-4 years of relevant experience with Bachelor's degree\",\"Less than 2 years of experience with Master's degree\"],\"location\":[\"Remote\"],\"requirements\":[\"Bachelor’s degree in computer science or a related field with 2-4 years of relevant experience or a Master’s degree with less than 2 years of experience.\",\"Experience with Java programming language.\",\"Experience with React.\",\"Experience with Web development and commonly used front-end tools and languages (HTML, CSS, JavaScript).\",\"Experience with Linux.\",\"Experience with version control systems such as Git or Subversion.\",\"Experience with common development tools and IDEs (Eclipse, VS Code, etc.).\",\"Knowledge of AI-assisted software development tools and workflows (i.e. Claude Code, Codex, etc.).\",\"Knowledge of Cloud-based systems.\",\"Knowledge of unit testing tools such as Junit and Mockito.\",\"Understanding of sound software development principles and practices.\",\"Ability to plan and prioritize personal tasking.\",\"Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing.\",\"Independent thinker, capable of performing high quality work, both independently and with a team in a fast-moving environment.\",\"Ability to obtain SF-85 Public Trust suitability determination.\",\"US citizenship required.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Design and implement software solutions independently.\",\"Work closely with systems engineering, product delivery, and DevSecOps teams.\",\"Develop containerized applications within an Agile/SAFe environment.\",\"Write, test, debug, and maintain source code.\",\"Actively participate in daily stand-ups, Release Planning, and other team activities.\",\"Write and execute unit and functional tests.\",\"Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues in lab and operational environments.\",\"Provide support for system engineering, test engineering, and system owner teams.\"],\"skills\":[\"Java\",\"React\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"JavaScript\",\"Linux\",\"Git\",\"Subversion\",\"Eclipse\",\"VS Code\",\"AI-assisted software development tools\",\"Cloud-based systems\",\"Junit\",\"Mockito\",\"Agile/SAFe framework\",\"RESTful API\",\"JSON\",\"XML\",\"XSD\",\"Spring Framework\",\"Spring Security\",\"Spring Boot\",\"Python\",\"Ansible playbooks\",\"YAML\",\"Linux shell scripting\",\"DevSecOps practices\",\"CI/CD pipelines\",\"MongoDB\",\"Air traffic control\",\"Flight services\"],\"work_type\":[\"Full-time\"]}},{\"id\":\"b55b80c1-8a24-4444-a83f-7a9a8ca89ceb\",\"source_id\":\"2415785475\",\"obfuscated_id\":42201130,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Aiimi\",\"job_url\":\"https://aiimi.careers.hibob.com/jobs/41e8d4ca-d4a5-4a6b-bcff-c6c9d6f6a6c9\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-15T15:16:07.433127Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"BKM, GB\",\"BKM, GBR\",\"BKM, United Kingdom\",\"Buckinghamshire, GB\",\"Buckinghamshire, GBR\",\"Buckinghamshire, United Kingdom\",\"GB\",\"GBR\",\"Milton Keynes, BKM, GB\",\"Milton Keynes, BKM, GBR\",\"Milton Keynes, BKM, United Kingdom\",\"Milton Keynes, Buckinghamshire, GB\",\"Milton Keynes, Buckinghamshire, GBR\",\"Milton Keynes, Buckinghamshire, United Kingdom\",\"United Kingdom\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"272fc253-9a78-44ef-bc4a-85bdafc5626a\",\"company_image_id\":\"mluxt12bio6agpbg97ni\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"GBP\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":45000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":70000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"NodeJS\",\"C#\",\"Angular\",\"React\",\"TypeScript\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"API Design\",\"Python\",\"Azure\",\"AWS\",\"GCP\",\"CI/CD\",\"Docker\",\"ElasticSearch\",\"Agile\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Aiimi is a British technology and services company delivering trusted, transformational AI for the enterprise. Through our Workplace AI platform and expert consulting in data, digital, and AI, we help complex businesses unlock the full value of their data and adopt AI at scale. From national security and critical infrastructure to leading GSIs and the world’s most prestigious luxury brands, our customers rely on Aiimi for rapid time to value, peer-to-peer relationships, and technology that sets the global standard.\\n\\nAs a Software Developer within Aiimi Software, you will play a key role in the development, and ongoing evolution of our Workplace AI platform and associated products.\\n\\nThis is a hands-on engineering role for someone who enjoys solving complex technical problems, contributing to the growth of a core product, improving platform quality, and contributing to architectural and design decisions. You will work within a cross-functional product team, collaborating closely with engineers, QA, product managers, and data specialists to deliver reliable, scalable, and secure software.\\n * Design, build, and maintain high-quality software components across frontend, backend, and API layers.\\n * Write clean, maintainable, and well-tested code aligned with agreed engineering standards and best practices.\\n * Participate in architectural discussions and help shape technical solutions that support scalability, performance, and security.\\n * Collaborate closely with QA engineers to embed quality, testability, and automation throughout the development lifecycle.\\n * Actively contribute to sprint planning, estimation, and delivery within an Agile environment.\\n * Investigate and resolve complex defects, performance issues, and technical debt.\\n * Contribute to CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, and deployment processes.\\n * Promote continuous improvement in engineering practices, tooling, and ways of working.\\n\\nEssential:\\n \\n\\n * 3+ years of professional experience in software development roles.\\n * Experience developing applications using NodeJS \\u0026 C# \\n * Experience building frontend applications using Angular, React TypeScript, HTML, and CSS.\\n * Experience designing and consuming APIs\\n * Experience or exposure to Python, particularly in data-driven or AI-adjacent systems.\\n * Understanding of modern software engineering practices and tooling, including Visual Studio, Jira, Git and Agile delivery.\\n * Experience using AI tools such as GitHub Copilot, or Cursor.\\n * Hands-on experience working with cloud platforms (e.g. Azure, AWS, GCP)\\n * Experience contributing to or maintaining CI/CD pipelines (e.g. GitHub Pipelines).\\n * Ability to troubleshoot and resolve issues across application code, containers, and runtime environments.\\n * Strong communication and collaboration skills.\\n\\n \\nDesirable:\\n \\n\\n * Experience developing[AL1]  or running applications on Windows and Linux.\\n * Understanding of Redux state management patterns (e.g. NgRx) and real-time, event-driven communication using messaging or socket-based technologies (e.g. SignalR, Socket.IO).\\n * Experience with Docker, including building, running, and troubleshooting containerised applications.\\n * Experience working with ElasticSearch \\n * Interest in building enterprise-grade AI, data, or knowledge-driven platforms.\\n\\nBenefits Package\\n\\n * Life Insurance\\n * Income Protection\\n * Pension Contribution 9% pension\\n * Private Healthcare Full private healthcare\\n\\nMental Wellbeing Support\\n\\n * Private Counselling\\n * Mental Wellbeing Tools\\n\\nVolunteer Days\\n\\n * Community Engagement: Three days per year to volunteer with organisations of your choice.\\n\\nConnectivity Allowance\\n\\n * Monthly Allowance to support remote working.\\n\\nWellbeing Allowance\\n\\n * Yearly Allowance: £400 per year to spend on activities that support your physical and mental wellbeing.\\n\\nAnnual Leave\\n\\n * Standard Leave: 25 days of annual leave plus Bank Holidays.\\n * Additional Leave: Earn an extra day of annual leave for every two years of employment with Aiimi.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Aiimi is a British technology and services company delivering trusted, transformational AI for the enterprise.\",\"Through our Workplace AI platform and expert consulting in data, digital, and AI, we help complex businesses unlock the full value of their data and adopt AI at scale.\",\"From national security and critical infrastructure to leading GSIs and the world’s most prestigious luxury brands, our customers rely on Aiimi for rapid time to value, peer-to-peer relationships, and technology that sets the global standard.\"],\"about_role\":\"As a Software Developer within Aiimi Software, you will play a key role in the development and ongoing evolution of our Workplace AI platform and associated products. This is a hands-on engineering role for someone who enjoys solving complex technical problems, contributing to the growth of a core product, improving platform quality, and contributing to architectural and design decisions. You will work within a cross-functional product team, collaborating closely with engineers, QA, product managers, and data specialists to deliver reliable, scalable, and secure software.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[\"Life Insurance\",\"Income Protection\",\"Pension Contribution 9% pension\",\"Full private healthcare\",\"Private Counselling\",\"Mental Wellbeing Tools\",\"Three volunteer days per year\",\"Monthly Connectivity Allowance\",\"£400 yearly Wellbeing Allowance\",\"25 days of annual leave plus Bank Holidays\",\"Additional leave earned for tenure\"],\"education_level\":[],\"equal_opportunity\":[],\"experience_level\":[\"3+ years\"],\"location\":[\"Remote\"],\"requirements\":[\"3+ years of professional experience in software development roles.\",\"Experience developing applications using NodeJS \\u0026 C#.\",\"Experience building frontend applications using Angular, React TypeScript, HTML, and CSS.\",\"Experience designing and consuming APIs.\",\"Experience or exposure to Python, particularly in data-driven or AI-adjacent systems.\",\"Understanding of modern software engineering practices and tooling, including Visual Studio, Jira, Git and Agile delivery.\",\"Experience using AI tools such as GitHub Copilot, or Cursor.\",\"Hands-on experience working with cloud platforms (e.g. Azure, AWS, GCP).\",\"Experience contributing to or maintaining CI/CD pipelines (e.g. GitHub Pipelines).\",\"Ability to troubleshoot and resolve issues across application code, containers, and runtime environments.\",\"Strong communication and collaboration skills.\",\"Experience developing or running applications on Windows and Linux.\",\"Understanding of Redux state management patterns (e.g. NgRx) and real-time, event-driven communication using messaging or socket-based technologies (e.g. SignalR, Socket.IO).\",\"Experience with Docker, including building, running, and troubleshooting containerised applications.\",\"Experience working with ElasticSearch.\",\"Interest in building enterprise-grade AI, data, or knowledge-driven platforms.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Design, build, and maintain high-quality software components across frontend, backend, and API layers.\",\"Write clean, maintainable, and well-tested code aligned with agreed engineering standards and best practices.\",\"Participate in architectural discussions and help shape technical solutions that support scalability, performance, and security.\",\"Collaborate closely with QA engineers to embed quality, testability, and automation throughout the development lifecycle.\",\"Actively contribute to sprint planning, estimation, and delivery within an Agile environment.\",\"Investigate and resolve complex defects, performance issues, and technical debt.\",\"Contribute to CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, and deployment processes.\",\"Promote continuous improvement in engineering practices, tooling, and ways of working.\"],\"skills\":[\"NodeJS\",\"C#\",\"Angular\",\"React\",\"TypeScript\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"API design\",\"API consumption\",\"Python\",\"Visual Studio\",\"Jira\",\"Git\",\"Agile\",\"GitHub Copilot\",\"Cursor\",\"Azure\",\"AWS\",\"GCP\",\"CI/CD\",\"GitHub Pipelines\",\"Windows\",\"Linux\",\"Redux\",\"NgRx\",\"SignalR\",\"Socket.IO\",\"Docker\",\"ElasticSearch\"],\"work_type\":[\"Full-time\"]}},{\"id\":\"7349bbc6-7971-48a1-acdf-a2d3e0a5e2ed\",\"source_id\":\"2414554179\",\"obfuscated_id\":42150754,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"State of Oregon\",\"job_url\":\"https://oregon.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/SOR_External_Career_Site/job/Salem--ODOT--Transportation-Building/Software-Developer_REQ-208378\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-15T00:19:13.778351Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"OR, US\",\"OR, USA\",\"OR, United States\",\"Oregon, US\",\"Oregon, USA\",\"Oregon, United States\",\"Salem, OR, US\",\"Salem, OR, USA\",\"Salem, OR, United States\",\"Salem, Oregon, US\",\"Salem, Oregon, USA\",\"Salem, Oregon, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"02f57eff-5a7e-2493-0d2d-2d61d3186ce7\",\"company_image_id\":\"6488554e4b4d4ff48da21876036d9a1d\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":6182,\"salary_max_value\":9361,\"salary_unit_text\":\"MONTH\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":6182,\"ai_salary_max_value\":9361,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"MONTH\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\".NET\",\"C#\",\"SQL Server\",\"API development\",\"SOAP\",\"RESTful\",\"System analysis\",\"Database management\",\"Performance tuning\",\"Debugging\",\"Technical documentation\",\"Software integration\",\"Batch processing\",\"UI components\",\"Data mapping\",\"Automation\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Initial Posting Date: \\n10/14/2026\\nApplication Deadline:\\n10/21/2026\\nAgency:\\nDepartment of Transportation\\nSalary Range:\\n$6,182 - $9,361\\nPosition Type:\\nEmployee\\nPosition Title:\\nSoftware Developer\\nJob Description:\\nInformation Systems Specialist 6 – Software Developer\\nOregon Department of Transportation\\nSupport Services Division – Information Systems Branch \\nDMV Driver Application Services \\nSalem\\n\\nThe role: \\nWe’re looking for a software developer to join our Oregon Driver and Motor Vehicles (DMV) Driver Application Services team! In this role, you will build and maintain secure, reliable DMV applications that translate business needs into quality software. You’ll also contribute to system enhancements and integrations, and ensure stable, high performing solutions. Apply today!\\nWe provide a safe and reliable multimodal transportation system that connects people and helps Oregon's communities and economy thrive. We encourage people from all backgrounds and abilities to apply for our positions.\\nBefore applying, visit our applicant information website to learn more about our process. If you are a current State of Oregon employee, you must apply through your employee Workday profile.\\n\\nA day in the life:\\nWrite production quality code to implement core services, Application Programming Interfaces (APIs), integrations, batch jobs, SQL query writing and optimization, and User Interface (UI) components.\\nCreate tests cases, integrate them into releases and raise coverage on critical paths and failure prone areas.\\nPerform complex debugging and performance tuning using profilers, tracing and metrics.\\nOptimize queries, memory, concurrency and Input/Output (I/O) while protecting data integrity.\\nEstimate and sequence technical work, identify tradeoffs and recommend options when scope, schedule and risk conflict.\\nProvide production support including prioritizing incidents, resolving defects, implementing hotfixes and participating in release decisions.\\nMonitor and analyze logs and metrics, perform root cause analysis and implement preventive improvements and automation.\\nDesign and maintain database queries, objects, stored procedures and data mappings.\\nCreate and validate extracts and reports needed to support downstream consumers and statutory requirements.\\nCreate and maintain user and support documentation, assist with escalations and resolve issues.\\nCommunicate technical status, risks and options to technical and non-technical audiences.\\nMay require overnight travel and working after hours.\\nHybrid work options available – in office work is required typically once or twice a month but is based on business needs.\\nTo request a copy of the position description, which includes all duties and working conditions, please email ODOTRecruitment@odot.oregon.gov.\\n\\nWhat’s in it for you:\\nWork/life balance, 11 paid holidays a year, flexible work schedules, paid leave and so much more. Learn more about working at the Oregon Department of Transportation and the benefits we offer.\\nComprehensive and equitable base salary offer within the listed range. Through an equal pay assessment, we will determine the salary offer using the information you provide in your submitted application materials. Please ensure your application materials are detailed, accurate and reflect your skills, experience (paid and unpaid) and education as they relate to the position when applying. \\nThe salary range listed is the non-PERS monthly salary range. If you are already a participating PERS member or once you become PERS eligible, the salary range will increase by 6.95%.\\nPublic Service Loan Forgiveness opportunity!\\n\\nWant to know about new job postings? Subscribe to receive weekly email notifications!\\nMinimum qualifications:\\nFive (5) years of information systems experience in: application development or application production support.\\n\\nOR\\n\\nAn associate's degree in computer science, information technology, or related field OR\\ncompletion of a two (2) year accredited vocational training program in information technology or related field;\\nAND\\nthree (3) years of information systems experience in: application development or application production support.\\n\\nOR\\n\\nA bachelor's degree in information technology, computer science, or related field AND one (1) year of information systems experience in: application development or application production support.\\n\\nWhat we’d like to see:\\nIf you have these attributes, let us know in your application materials! It's how we will choose whom to move forward! You do not need to have all these qualities to be eligible for this position. We may also use transferable skills, experience and education to help us decide who will move forward.\\nAdvanced level experience using .NET, C# and SQL Server.\\nExperience in application development and system analysis.\\nExperience building and maintaining hybrid solutions such as Commercial Off the Shelf (COTS) solutions with customizations including configuration, development, testing and migration activities.\\nExpertise developing and maintaining Application Programming Interfaces (API) such as SOAP or RESTful for integration with systems that support core business functions.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\nComplete the following required steps:\\nFill out the application or attach a resume. Please contact the recruiter under the ‘Need help?’ section if you have any questions about how to fill out the experience fields or to attach a document. Your submitted experience fields or attached resume must include dates (MM/YYYY) for each employer.\\nComplete questionnaire. Answer the checkbox-style questions before submitting your application.\\nAfter you submit your application, please respond to the public records request authorization and gender identity questionnaire. This screen will come after you submit and will complete the process. If you are a current State of Oregon employee, the tasks will come to your Workday inbox.\\nIf you are a veteran or Oregon National Guard servicemember, you may receive preference. The task to upload your documents will be available after you submit your application. For privacy reasons, please do not attach your military service document(s) to your application or combine it with any other required document attachments.\\nNeed help?\\nFor questions, call 503-910-6372 or email ODOTRecruitmentCC@odot.oregon.gov.\\n\\nAdditional information:\\nWe do not offer visa sponsorship. If you are hired, you will be required to fill out the US Department of Homeland Security’s I-9 form confirming you are able to work in the US. We are not an E-Verify participating employer, and we are unable to proceed if E-Verify participation is required [e.g., STEM Optional Practical Training (OPT) Extension].\\nThe State of Oregon does not request or require your age, date of birth, attendance or graduation dates from an education institution during the application process.\\nWe may use this recruitment to fill multiple or future vacancies.\\nWe will conduct name-based and fingerprint-based criminal background checks on final candidates under consideration for this position. All applicants may be subject to additional pre-employment check(s) such as driver license, LEDS (Law Enforcement Data System), and/or education verification as required for the position.\\nYou will be represented by the Service Employees International Union (SEIU).\\n\\nODOT is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, age, national origin, disability, sexual orientation or any other class protected by state or federal laws in admission or access to our programs, services, activities, hiring, and employment practices. Applicants with a disability may request a reasonable accommodation during the application process. For questions, concerns, or complaints regarding EEO/AA/ADA, contact 1-877-336-6368 (1-877-EEO-ODOT). This information can be made available in an alternative format by contacting ODOT Recruitment at 503-986-3700. Oregon Relay Service can be reached by calling 7-1-1.\\n#LI-ODOT\\n#LI-DNP\\n#LI-Hybrid\"},{\"id\":\"4aa55d59-c2e8-4a0e-9c9c-9834eb39454b\",\"source_id\":\"2413841963\",\"obfuscated_id\":42089207,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"MANTECH\",\"job_url\":\"https://careers.mantech.com/en_US/careers/JobDetail/Software-Developer/66533\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-14T17:16:09.200704Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Fort Detrick, MD, US\",\"Fort Detrick, MD, USA\",\"Fort Detrick, MD, United States\",\"Fort Detrick, Maryland, US\",\"Fort Detrick, Maryland, USA\",\"Fort Detrick, Maryland, United States\",\"MD, US\",\"MD, USA\",\"MD, United States\",\"Maryland, US\",\"Maryland, USA\",\"Maryland, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"3309451a-a9d5-ea52-5ef6-61049d00878b\",\"company_image_id\":\"j7dniilhyq3p2ak4xono\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"salary_min_value\":163100,\"salary_max_value\":289400,\"salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":163100,\"ai_salary_max_value\":289400,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"YEAR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Java\",\"SpringBoot\",\"Angular\",\"JavaScript\",\"Full Stack Development\",\"RESTful APIs\",\"Agile\",\"SCRUM\",\"SAFe\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Relational Databases\",\"NoSQL\",\"Microservices\",\"Python\",\"Cloud Computing\",\"Containerization\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"DESCRIPTION \\u0026 REQUIREMENTS\\n\\nShape the future of defense with MANTECH! Join a team dedicated to safeguarding our nation through advanced tech and innovative solutions. Since 1968, we’ve been a trusted partner to the Department of Defense, delivering cutting-edge projects that make a real impact. Dive into exciting opportunities in Cybersecurity, IT, Data Analytics and more. Propel your career forward and be part of something extraordinary. Your journey starts now—protect and innovate with MANTECH!\\n\\nMANTECH seeks a motivated, career and customer-oriented Software Developer, Subject Matter Expert to join our team in Ft Detrick, MD. This position is on-site three days per week but expanded telework options are available on a case-by-case basis.\\n\\nWe are seeking a motivated, mission-oriented SME Software Developer to work with our MEDLOG IT PMO customer at Ft. Detrick in Frederick, MD.  This detail-oriented individual will be an imperative part of the LogiCole Software Engineering team and is obsessed with accuracy, and able to accept critical feedback because they are always looking to learn, grow, and produce the highest quality outcome.\\n\\nResponsibilities include but are not limited to:\\n\\n * Participate in agile team, backlog grooming, story sizing sessions.\\n * Develop code in accordance with cybersecurity standards, design standards, 508 standards and style guides; any deviations from the standards require prior approval.\\n * Document designs, unit tests and code reviews.\\n * Participate in product evaluations.\\n\\nMinimum Qualifications:\\n\\n * Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Data Science, Information Systems, or Computer Science from a nationally accredited institution. If the candidate does not have the required degree, 6 year’s experience in a related field in addition to one of the following current certifications are required: Cloud+, GICSP, SSCP, Security+, GSEC, FITSP-O, GFACT, CASP+, CCNP Security, or CCSP\\n * Additional 10 years of experience with Full Stack Development, implementing and consuming RESTful APIs\\n * At least 5 years of experience working on an Agile team and following Agile processes SCRUM and/or Scaled Agile Framework (SAFe)\\n * Solid Java 17+ skills and experience with EAP’s (JBoss/Wildfly) and/or SpringBoot\\n * Experience in building front-end application using Angular and JavaScript\\n * Experience using relational and/or NoSQL database systems\\n\\nPreferred Qualifications:\\n\\n * Experience with mTLS, CAC, PIV, OIDC, SAML Authentication\\n * Experience with Messaging Systems (ActiveMQ, Artemis, Kafka)\\n * Experience using Artificial Intelligent code assistance to create new code, update existing code, troubleshoot code defects, create automated unit tests, etc.\\n * Experience with enterprise-level application development\\n * Knowledge of design patterns applicable to Java EE solutions; knowledge of design patterns common to Angular/JavaScript solutions\\n * Experience with containerization technologies such as Docker, Kubernetes, etc as well as experience or certifications with cloud hosting solutions, particularly AWS\\n * Understands Bash or PowerShell, Python 3+ experience and Microservice architecture / development experience\\n\\nClearance Requirements:\\n\\n * Must be a U.S. Citizen and be able to obtain and maintain a Public Trust prior to starting.\\n * Will be subject to a Tier 2 Investigation for DoD Common Access Card (CAC) eligibility only.\\n * Candidates who have recently completed T2 investigations are a plus.\\n\\n \\n\\nPhysical Requirements:\\n\\n * The person in this position frequently communicates with co-workers, management and customers, which may involve delivering presentations; must be able to exchange accurate information in these situations. The person in this position will need to be able to operate a computer and other office productivity machinery, such as a calculator, copy machine and computer printer.\\n\\n \\n\\nThe projected compensation range for this position is $163,100.00-$289,400.00. There are differentiating factors that can impact a final salary/hourly rate, including, but not limited to, Contract Wage Determination, relevant work experience, skills and competencies that align to the specified role, geographic location (For Remote Opportunities), education and certifications as well as Federal Government Contract Labor categories.  In addition, MANTECH invests in its employees beyond just compensation.  MANTECH’s benefits offerings include, dependent upon position, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Paid Time Off, Holiday Pay, short-term and long-term Disability, Retirement and Savings, Learning and Development opportunities, wellness programs as well as other optional benefit elections.\\n\\nMANTECH considers all qualified applicants for employment without regard to disability or veteran status or any other status protected under any federal, state, or local law or regulation.\\n\\nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to apply for a position with MANTECH, please email us at careers@mantech.com and provide your name and contact information.\\n\\nGENERAL INFORMATION\\n\\nRequisition #\\nR71347\\nLocations\\nUSA-MD-Fort Detrick\\nPosting Date\\n10/14/2026\\nSecurity Clearance Required\\nPublic Trust/Suitability\\nRemote Type\\nHybrid\\nTime Type\\nFull time\"},{\"id\":\"4be2d32e-a742-4aa3-8150-ea266325fb09\",\"source_id\":\"2413514156\",\"obfuscated_id\":42071999,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"SmartDok AS\",\"job_url\":\"https://smartdokas.teamtailor.com/jobs/8544621-software-developer\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-14T14:17:57.307986Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Alta, Troms og Finnmark, NO\",\"Alta, Troms og Finnmark, NOR\",\"Alta, Troms og Finnmark, Norway\",\"Lysaker, Viken, NO\",\"Lysaker, Viken, NOR\",\"Lysaker, Viken, Norway\",\"NO\",\"NOR\",\"Norway\",\"Troms og Finnmark, NO\",\"Troms og Finnmark, NOR\",\"Troms og Finnmark, Norway\",\"Tromso, Troms og Finnmark, NO\",\"Tromso, Troms og Finnmark, NOR\",\"Tromso, Troms og Finnmark, Norway\",\"Viken, NO\",\"Viken, NOR\",\"Viken, Norway\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"ee3ea73e-1588-4820-9e0f-e7e401b1abe5\",\"company_image_id\":\"vlfdhdewoaobt1dmtqgu\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"NOK\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":600000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":850000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Software development\",\"Infrastructure\",\"System integration\",\"Automation\",\"API development\",\"Cloud computing\",\"CRM\",\"Data modeling\",\"CI/CD\",\"Infrastructure as code\",\"AI\",\"Troubleshooting\",\"Databases\",\"Billing systems\",\"Subscription management\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Software Developer\\nVi søker en erfaren og teknisk sterk seniorutvikler med kompetanse og erfaring innen drift og infrastruktur til en fast 100 % stilling.\\nDu kan ha kontorsted i Tromsø, i Oslo eller på hovedkontoret vårt i Alta.\\n\\nOm rollen\\nDu vil inngå i teamet som sørger for at kundedataene stemmer og at de interne systemene og produktene våre fungerer sammen. Det gjelder alt fra kontoadministrasjon og provisjonering til CRM (HubSpot) og abonnementsstyring (Younium). Hovedvekten i rollen ligger på integrasjoner, automatisering, drift og infrastruktur. Som engasjert utvikler vil du også kunne bidra i andre produktområder. Kompetanse innen drift og infrastruktur er viktig fordi du skal inngå i bakvaktordningen vår.\\nVi er ikke så opptatt av hvilke konkrete teknologier du kan fra før, fordi vi mener at kompetanse har stor overføringsverdi.\\nAI er en essensiell del av SmartDoks arbeidsmetode for produktutvikling og er et av våre viktigste satsingsområder. Vi forventer at du bruker AI som en naturlig del av arbeidet og at du har lyst til å gå foran når vi tar i bruk nye muligheter.\\n\\nDette skal du gjøre\\nTa ansvar for drift og videreutvikling av utvalgte interne systemer.\\nBygge og vedlikeholde integrasjoner og automatisering mellom CRM, abonnementer, provisjonering og fakturering. Det er her mesteparten av programmeringen skjer.\\nHøyt fokus på datakvalitet og på å jobbe mot manuelle og feilutsatte ledd fra signert avtale til fakturert tjeneste.\\nVære teknisk sparringspartner for salg, finans og kundesuksess og gjøre behovene deres om til løsninger som tåler drift over tid.\\nInngå i bakvaktordning og bidra til å håndtere hendelser i våre løsninger.\\n\\nDette må du ha\\nUtdanning innen informatikk eller tilsvarende. Lang erfaring fra relevante tekniske roller kan i enkelte tilfeller veie opp for manglende utdanning.\\nMinimum 3 års erfaring med programmering og drift av systemer i produksjon, gjerne i skyen. Du har selv hatt ansvar for at noe du har bygget, faktisk kjører.\\nErfaring med å bruke AI aktivt i arbeidshverdagen, for eksempel til koding, feilsøking og automatisering.\\nGode norsk- og engelskkunnskaper, både muntlig og skriftlig.\\nDette ser vi gjerne\\nErfaring med API-er, systemintegrasjon og datamodellering.\\nErfaring med forretningssystemer som CRM, ERP, abonnement eller fakturering.\\nForståelse for hvordan en kundeavtale blir til inntekt (lead-to-cash).\\nErfaring med infrastruktur som kode, CI/CD eller dataplattformer.\\nHvem du er\\nDu ser helheten og tenker på hvordan systemene henger sammen, ikke bare på oppgaven foran deg.\\nDu er «lat», men effektiv: Gjør du noe manuelt to ganger, automatiserer du det.\\nDu er selvgående og ryddig og tar ansvar for at ting fungerer hele veien.\\nDu snakker like godt med finans og salg som med utviklere.\\nHvorfor velge SmartDok\\nHos oss setter du spor i et selskap i vekst, og du har tryggheten fra Visma-konsernet.\\nDet du får\\nLønn etter erfaring og bidrag, ikke etter faste ansiennitetstrinn\\nGode forsikrings- og pensjonsordninger og firmabonus\\nTreningsgodtgjørelse du kan bruke på klær, utstyr eller medlemskap\\nGodtgjørelse til jobbrelatert utstyr og tjenester, så du kan jobbe med verktøy som passer deg\\nHverdagen\\nDu har påvirkningskraft. Det du bidrar med, merkes.\\nDu får en ekstra time i uka til fysisk aktivitet i arbeidstiden.\\nDu kan jobbe hjemmefra inntil to dager i uka.\\nDu jobber fra flotte kontorlokaler i Alta, Tromsø eller Oslo.\\nFolkene\\nDu får god opplæring og støtte fra dyktige kolleger.\\nMiljøet er inkluderende, kunnskapsrikt og sosialt, og vi heier på hverandre.\\n\\nSpørsmål om stillingen?\\nTa kontakt med HR Advisor Gerd-Kathrine Winther: gerd@smartdok.com\"},{\"id\":\"72f6226e-17be-4125-a4c8-71b61cee47b8\",\"source_id\":\"2417894251\",\"obfuscated_id\":42316055,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Park Place Technologies\",\"job_url\":\"https://recruiting.ultipro.com/PAR1035PPTL/JobBoard/e104637a-c3c6-4682-96d2-d7cc2662dc13/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=1f500b28-076a-44e0-acb0-9650b6fb3b50\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-16T14:19:19.226989Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Highland Heights, OH, US\",\"Highland Heights, OH, USA\",\"Highland Heights, OH, United States\",\"Highland Heights, Ohio, US\",\"Highland Heights, Ohio, USA\",\"Highland Heights, Ohio, United States\",\"OH, US\",\"OH, USA\",\"OH, United States\",\"Ohio, US\",\"Ohio, USA\",\"Ohio, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"451baade-0606-f793-0544-4f8cea7abafc\",\"company_image_id\":\"gr1dre2wy1q2radndevm\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":110000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Python\",\"C++\",\"Software Development\",\"Technical Documentation\",\"Unit Testing\",\"Automated Testing\",\"Problem Solving\",\"Linux\",\"Visual Studio\",\"Java\",\"JavaScript\",\"Software Architecture\",\"Requirement Analysis\",\"Code Review\",\"System Testing\",\"Integration Testing\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Software Developer\\n\\nThe Software Developer is responsible for the analysis, design, implementation,\\ntesting and maintenance of professionally engineered Network Analytics software\\nsystems and supporting internal tools, as required, to fulfil the needs of the\\nbusiness, and which meet or exceed PPT’s quality standards.\\n\\n \\n\\nWhat you’ll be doing:\\n\\n * Acquire a thorough understanding of, and comply with, ParkView’s software\\n   development life cycle and its associated processes.\\n * Work with Development Manager and Product Management to establish the\\n   requirements for new features and feature enhancements, and then translate\\n   into a specification, documenting as appropriate.\\n * Must be able to document product development, project and user tasks.\\n * Work with Software Architects to conceive solution(s) to meet the\\n   requirements and, where necessary, investigate the feasibility of the\\n   solution(s). Document the solutions and the results of any investigation, as\\n   appropriate.\\n * Produce required technical design documentation and ensure peer review.\\n * Implement software component(s) as per the design, in a timescale agreed with\\n   the Development Manager.\\n * Carry out appropriate code-level testing, and create automated test scripts /\\n   unit tests, as agreed with the Development Manager and Software Architects.\\n * Work with QA to create and review test plans and, at times, help to execute\\n   functional, integration and system testing.\\n * Participate in the resolution of issues and software bugs identified before\\n   and after release, either internally or by customers in the field.\\n\\n \\n\\nWhat we’re looking for:\\n\\n * 1-3 years’ work experience in software development field or equivalent\\n   experience required.\\n * Must be able to work under time sensitive deadlines that have a large impact\\n   to the business.\\n * Experience using Python, C++ required.\\n * Have an analytical mind and a natural aptitude for problem solving.\\n * Have a positive attitude towards learning.\\n * Demonstrate good written and verbal communication skills.\\n * Be a proactive team player.\\n\\n \\n\\nBonus Points:\\n\\n * 3-5 years’ work experience in the software development field or equivalent\\n   experience.\\n * Experience using Linux, Visual Studio, Java or Java Script.\\n * Commercial Work experience.\\n\\n \\n\\nEducation:\\n\\n * Bachelor’s Degree required.\\n\\n \\n\\nTravel:\\n\\n * 10%\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[],\"about_role\":\"The Software Developer is responsible for the analysis, design, implementation, testing, and maintenance of professionally engineered Network Analytics software systems and supporting internal tools to fulfill business needs and meet quality standards.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[],\"education_level\":[\"Bachelor’s Degree required.\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[],\"experience_level\":[\"1-3 years’ work experience in software development field or equivalent experience required.\",\"3-5 years’ work experience in the software development field or equivalent experience.\"],\"location\":[],\"requirements\":[\"Must be able to work under time-sensitive deadlines that have a large impact on the business.\",\"Have an analytical mind and a natural aptitude for problem-solving.\",\"Have a positive attitude towards learning.\",\"Demonstrate good written and verbal communication skills.\",\"Be a proactive team player.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Acquire a thorough understanding of, and comply with, ParkView’s software development life cycle and its associated processes.\",\"Work with Development Manager and Product Management to establish requirements for new features and feature enhancements, and translate them into specifications.\",\"Document product development, project, and user tasks.\",\"Work with Software Architects to conceive solutions to meet requirements and investigate feasibility.\",\"Document solutions and investigation results.\",\"Produce required technical design documentation and ensure peer review.\",\"Implement software components as per the design within agreed timescales.\",\"Carry out appropriate code-level testing and create automated test scripts/unit tests.\",\"Work with QA to create and review test plans and assist in executing functional, integration, and system testing.\",\"Participate in the resolution of issues and software bugs identified before and after release.\"],\"skills\":[\"Python\",\"C++\",\"Linux\",\"Visual Studio\",\"Java\",\"Java Script\"],\"work_type\":[]}},{\"id\":\"2b5d4c0a-2aa6-4695-8ec6-bf358495c008\",\"source_id\":\"2419740774\",\"obfuscated_id\":42437548,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"BCC-NIH\",\"job_url\":\"https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/bcc/jobs/5880038003\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-17T11:18:22.719914Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Bethesda, MD, US\",\"Bethesda, MD, USA\",\"Bethesda, MD, United States\",\"Bethesda, Maryland, US\",\"Bethesda, Maryland, USA\",\"Bethesda, Maryland, United States\",\"MD, US\",\"MD, USA\",\"MD, United States\",\"Maryland, US\",\"Maryland, USA\",\"Maryland, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":true,\"company_id\":\"048b9537-071d-43dd-92dd-8e19f3aca695\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":95000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":140000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Python\",\"GoLang\",\"C++\",\"Java\",\"JavaScript\",\"HTML5\",\"CSS3\",\"SQL\",\"XML\",\"JSON\",\"CSV\",\"ASN.1\",\"Git\",\"SVN\",\"Agile\",\"Software documentation\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Black Canyon Consulting (BCC) is searching for a Software Developer to support at the National Institutes of Health (NIH). This opportunity is full time in Bethesda, MD and/or remote work.\\nAs a Software Developer, you will contribute to development efforts that support the goals and initiatives of the product team and organization while learning Software Development practices from an experienced team. This work is performed under the guidance of the Technical Program Manager and the Technical Lead.\\nWe attract the best people in the business with our competitive benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision coverage, 401k plan with employer contribution, paid holidays, vacation, and tuition reimbursement. If you enjoy being a part of a high performing, professional service and technology focused organization, please apply today!\\nResponsibilities include:\\nWork with the Software Development team on front-end and back-end software development tasks\\nContribute to design discussions for new software development efforts\\nLearn Software Development practices from an experienced team\\nParticipate in software documentation activities with the team\\nWork as an integral part of an agile product team to deliver an unbelievably great user experience\\nQualifications:\\nThe ideal candidate may or may not be a United States citizen and must have at least a Bachelor or Master of Science degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or Engineering or equivalent work experience.\\nWe are looking for an individual with:\\nExperience developing software applications in Python\\nExperience developing software with GoLang, C++, and/or Java a plus\\nUnderstanding of front-end technologies, such as JavaScript, HTML5, and CSS3\\nExperience working with SQL databases\\nAbility to work with common structured documents (XML, JSON, CSV)\\nUnderstanding of ASN.1 a plus\\nExperience with version control systems like Git or SVN \\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills and team player\"},{\"id\":\"70a32142-87be-475e-8d30-ce165f7925c0\",\"source_id\":\"2414528276\",\"obfuscated_id\":42151979,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Capgemini\",\"job_url\":\"https://careers.capgemini.com/job/Singapore-Software-Developer/1447424233/\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-15T00:20:10.478089Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"SG\",\"SGP\",\"Singapore\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"a1d935af-1d49-55ef-2bf6-cbd1bf82af6d\",\"company_image_id\":\"d6183eef6c994ef1ae4d4d80f2701a8f\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"SGD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":60000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":120000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Full-stack development\",\"Angular\",\"Node.js\",\"Python\",\"RESTful API\",\"AWS\",\"Cloud-native services\",\"CI/CD\",\"DevSecOps\",\"Microservices\",\"Agile\",\"Software architecture\",\"Automated testing\",\"Database management\",\"Security scanning\",\"Problem-solving\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"About Capgemini\\nCapgemini is an AI-powered global business and technology transformation partner, delivering tangible business value. We imagine the future of organizations and make it real with AI, technology and people. With our strong heritage of nearly 60 years, we are a responsible and diverse group of over 420,000 team members in more than 50 countries. We deliver end-to-end services and solutions with our deep industry expertise and strong partner ecosystem, leveraging our capabilities across strategy, technology, design, engineering and business operations. The Group reported 2025 global revenues of €22.5 billion.Responsibilities\\n\\nDesign, develop, enhance, integrate, test and maintain the full-stack software applications, including frontend applications, backend services, APIs, databases and supporting components, using modern software engineering practices;\\nImplement, configure and integrate cloud-native services within the Government Commercial Cloud Amazon Web Services (GCC-AWS) environment, including compute, storage, database, networking, security, monitoring and integration services, to support the deployment and operation of the applications;\\nDevelop, maintain and improve the CI/CD and DevSecOps pipelines, including source control, automated build, testing, code quality analysis, security scanning, packaging and deployment across development, testing and production environments;\\nParticipate and contribute actively within an Agile software development environment, including sprint planning, backlog refinement, daily stand-ups, technical discussions, demonstrations and retrospectives, and delivering working software and other assigned deliverables iteratively in accordance with agreed sprint objectives;\\nTake ownership of assigned technical, project related tasks, and deliverables, including investigating and resolving technical issues, coordination, conducting troubleshooting and root-cause analysis, identifying technical risks and improvement opportunities, and implementing appropriate solutions in a timely manner;\\nCollaborate with product owners, business analysts, developers, architects, infrastructure and cybersecurity teams, vendors and other stakeholders to align technical activities, resolve issues and support successful delivery; and\\nParticipate in code and design reviews, maintain technical documentation, actively contribute to knowledge sharing and continuous improvement within the team.\\nRequirements\\n\\nPossess a recognised degree, diploma or equivalent qualification in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering or a related discipline, with relevant professional experience in full-stack software development;\\nDemonstrate strong full-stack engineering capabilities, including hands-on proficiency in Angular for frontend development, Node.js and Python for backend development, RESTful API design and integration, and database technologies;\\nDemonstrate strong software engineering capabilities, including software architecture, software design principles, automated testing, debugging, and the development of secure, scalable and maintainable applications;\\nDemonstrate strong hands-on experience developing and deploying applications on AWS, including the use and integration of compute, storage, database, networking, security and monitoring services;\\nDemonstrate experience designing and implementing cloud-native, event-driven and microservices architectures, including synchronous and asynchronous integration patterns using APIs, message queues and other messaging technologies;\\nDemonstrate strong practical experience in modern CI/CD and DevSecOps practices, including Git-based source control, automated build and deployment pipelines, integration of testing and security controls into CI/CD pipelines, code quality management, vulnerability scanning, and controlled deployment across multiple environments;\\nDemonstrate practical experience working in Agile software development teams and applying sound software engineering practices, including incremental delivery, unit and integration testing, code reviews, secure coding, maintainable code, technical documentation and continuous improvement;\\nDemonstrate strong problem-solving, initiative and technical ownership, with the ability to work through ambiguity, independently investigate complex issues, identify root causes, propose appropriate solutions and drive assigned work to completion with minimal supervision; and\\nDemonstrate the ability to work independently and accountably, proactively communicate progress, risks, dependencies and impediments, escalate issues in a timely manner, and collaborate effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders to support successful delivery.\\nLet's talk about what's in it for you!\\n\\nPassionate people are Capgemini's Ace of Spades - join us to discover a career that will challenge, support and inspire you. Working at Capgemini you'll find the rewards are more than just financial. You will work alongside some very smart and inspiring people on exciting projects and you will also enjoy incredible benefits. We offer flexible work practices and 40 hours of self-development every year with a huge selection of learning opportunities to choose from.\\n\\nAs \\\"Architects of Positive Futures\\\", Capgemini actively supports the community in 3 ways:\\n\\nDiversity and Inclusion - we believe diversity of thought fuels excellence and innovation, which is why we positively encourage applications from suitably qualified candidates regardless of their gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, ability, intersex status or age. To support our commitment to diversity and inclusion, we celebrate special events and days of significance that are important to our employees such as Diwali, Bastille Day, Pride, IDAHOBIT, IWD and International day of people with Disabilities. Our Employee Resource Groups Women@Capgemini and OutFront support the grassroots passion of employees to drive our diversity agenda and effect change.\\n\\nDigital inclusion - at Capgemini we are using our skills to drive social impact initiatives focusing on helping society address the impact of the digital and automation revolution. We also provide employees with opportunities to give back to the community through charity projects and volunteer days.\\n\\nEnvironmental Sustainability - Capgemini joined the CDP's (Carbon Disclosure Project) prestigious \\\"A list\\\" for its commitment to the Net-Zero economy. We are focusing on helping our clients transform towards more sustainable business models and committing to reduce our own carbon emissions (GHG) by 20% per employee by 2020.\\n\\nRecognized by Ethisphere as one of the World's Most Ethical Companies for the last 8 years in a row, ethics and values are at the heart of Capgemini's corporate culture and business. Embedded in our DNA, our seven values - Honesty, Boldness, Trust, Team Spirit, Freedom, Fun and Modesty - have remained the same since company inception in 1967. To see how we bring these values to life, click here to listen to some of our employee’s stories.\\n\\nCome join us, bring your whole self to work, create new possibilities for you, your customers and your community and help us to be Architects of Positive Futures.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Capgemini is an AI-powered global business and technology transformation partner, delivering tangible business value.\",\"We imagine the future of organizations and make it real with AI, technology and people.\",\"With our strong heritage of nearly 60 years, we are a responsible and diverse group of over 420,000 team members in more than 50 countries.\",\"We deliver end-to-end services and solutions with our deep industry expertise and strong partner ecosystem, leveraging our capabilities across strategy, technology, design, engineering and business operations.\",\"The Group reported 2025 global revenues of €22.5 billion.\",\"As \\\"Architects of Positive Futures\\\", Capgemini actively supports the community in 3 ways: Diversity and Inclusion, Digital inclusion, and Environmental Sustainability.\",\"Recognized by Ethisphere as one of the World's Most Ethical Companies for the last 8 years in a row, ethics and values are at the heart of Capgemini's corporate culture and business.\",\"Our seven values - Honesty, Boldness, Trust, Team Spirit, Freedom, Fun and Modesty - have remained the same since company inception in 1967.\"],\"about_role\":\"Capgemini is an AI-powered global business and technology transformation partner. We deliver end-to-end services and solutions leveraging our capabilities across strategy, technology, design, engineering, and business operations.\",\"annual_salary\":[],\"benefits\":[\"Flexible work practices\",\"40 hours of self-development annually with a wide selection of learning opportunities\"],\"education_level\":[\"Recognized degree, diploma or equivalent qualification in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering or a related discipline\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"We believe diversity of thought fuels excellence and innovation, which is why we positively encourage applications from suitably qualified candidates regardless of their gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, ability, intersex status or age.\",\"To support our commitment to diversity and inclusion, we celebrate special events and days of significance that are important to our employees such as Diwali, Bastille Day, Pride, IDAHOBIT, IWD and International day of people with Disabilities.\",\"Our Employee Resource Groups Women@Capgemini and OutFront support the grassroots passion of employees to drive our diversity agenda and effect change.\"],\"experience_level\":[],\"location\":[],\"requirements\":[\"Possess a recognized degree, diploma, or equivalent qualification in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or a related discipline, with relevant professional experience in full-stack software development.\",\"Demonstrate strong full-stack engineering capabilities, including proficiency in Angular, Node.js, Python, RESTful API design and integration, and database technologies.\",\"Demonstrate strong software engineering capabilities, including software architecture, design principles, automated testing, debugging, and the development of secure, scalable, and maintainable applications.\",\"Demonstrate strong hands-on experience developing and deploying applications on AWS, including the use and integration of compute, storage, database, networking, security, and monitoring services.\",\"Demonstrate experience designing and implementing cloud-native, event-driven, and microservices architectures, including synchronous and asynchronous integration patterns.\",\"Demonstrate strong practical experience in modern CI/CD and DevSecOps practices.\",\"Demonstrate practical experience working in Agile software development teams and applying sound software engineering practices.\",\"Demonstrate strong problem-solving, initiative, and technical ownership.\",\"Demonstrate the ability to work independently and accountably, communicate proactively, escalate issues timely, and collaborate effectively with stakeholders.\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Design, develop, enhance, integrate, test, and maintain full-stack software applications, including frontend, backend services, APIs, databases, and supporting components using modern software engineering practices.\",\"Implement, configure, and integrate cloud-native services within the Government Commercial Cloud Amazon Web Services (GCC-AWS) environment.\",\"Develop, maintain, and improve CI/CD and DevSecOps pipelines.\",\"Participate and contribute actively within an Agile software development environment.\",\"Take ownership of assigned technical and project-related tasks and deliverables.\",\"Collaborate with product owners, business analysts, developers, architects, infrastructure and cybersecurity teams, vendors, and other stakeholders.\",\"Participate in code and design reviews, maintain technical documentation, and contribute to knowledge sharing and continuous improvement.\"],\"skills\":[\"Angular\",\"Node.js\",\"Python\",\"RESTful API design and integration\",\"Database technologies\",\"Software architecture\",\"Software design principles\",\"Automated testing\",\"Debugging\",\"Secure application development\",\"Scalable application development\",\"Maintainable application development\",\"AWS\",\"Compute services\",\"Storage services\",\"Database services\",\"Networking services\",\"Security services\",\"Monitoring services\",\"Cloud-native architectures\",\"Event-driven architectures\",\"Microservices architectures\",\"Synchronous integration patterns\",\"Asynchronous integration patterns\",\"APIs\",\"Message queues\",\"Messaging technologies\",\"CI/CD practices\",\"DevSecOps practices\",\"Git-based source control\",\"Automated build pipelines\",\"Automated deployment pipelines\",\"Integration of testing into CI/CD\",\"Integration of security controls into CI/CD\",\"Code quality management\",\"Vulnerability scanning\",\"Controlled deployment\",\"Agile software development\",\"Incremental delivery\",\"Unit testing\",\"Integration testing\",\"Code reviews\",\"Secure coding\",\"Maintainable code\",\"Technical documentation\",\"Continuous improvement\",\"Problem-solving\",\"Initiative\",\"Technical ownership\",\"Communication\"],\"work_type\":[]}},{\"id\":\"28de6470-9478-4066-ac3c-6f7885277d6d\",\"source_id\":\"2412189596\",\"obfuscated_id\":42008484,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Scarborough Health Network\",\"job_url\":\"https://shn.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/SHN_External_Career_Site/job/Centenary-Hospital/Software-Developer_JR107284\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-13T22:18:50.745728Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"CA\",\"CAN\",\"Canada\",\"ON, CA\",\"ON, CAN\",\"ON, Canada\",\"Ontario, CA\",\"Ontario, CAN\",\"Ontario, Canada\",\"Toronto, ON, CA\",\"Toronto, ON, CAN\",\"Toronto, ON, Canada\",\"Toronto, Ontario, CA\",\"Toronto, Ontario, CAN\",\"Toronto, Ontario, Canada\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"71bb0d43-d2c2-4557-a228-e397ef9e20e7\",\"company_image_id\":\"yj5gdszubr4w0otenjkr\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"CAD\",\"salary_min_value\":51.427,\"salary_max_value\":59.618,\"salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"CAD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":51.427,\"ai_salary_max_value\":59.618,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"HOUR\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Python\",\"Full-stack development\",\"PostgreSQL\",\"AWS\",\"React\",\"Next.js\",\"DevOps\",\"CI/CD\",\"API development\",\"LLM integration\",\"Database management\",\"Authentication\",\"System monitoring\",\"Git\",\"UI/UX design\",\"Cloud infrastructure\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Job Number: JR107284\\nJob Title: Software Developer\\nJob Category: Professional\\nHospital Location: Centenary Site\\nJob Type: Temporary (Fixed Term), Full time\\nContract Duration: 8 months\\nNumber of Positions: 1\\nUnion:\\nMinimum - Maximum Hourly Rate: $51.427 - $59.618\\nHours: Days\\nAcross our three hospitals and eight satellite sites, Scarborough Health Network (SHN) is shaping the future of care. Our many programs and services are designed around the needs of one of Canada’s most vibrant and diverse communities. We are home to North America’s largest nephrology program, as well as the designated cardiac care and spine centre for Scarborough and surrounding communities to the east. We are proud to be a community-affiliated teaching site for the University of Toronto and partner with a number of other universities and colleges, helping to train the next generation of health care professionals. SHN is the recipient of the 2021 Excellence in Diversity and Inclusion Award, from the Canadian College of Health Leaders, for our leading edge work on Communities of Inclusion, Inclusion Calendar, Health Equity Certificate Program and much more. We are also proud to be named Canada’s Most Admired Corporate Cultures for 2023 and 2024! Learn more at shn.ca\\nJob Description:\\nThe Software Developer will primarily support the implementation and ongoing development of the Virtual Standardized Patient (VSP) platform within a college training environment. Under the direction of the Principal Investigator and the research management team, this position focuses on integrating, deploying, testing, maintaining, and enhancing the platform and its supporting services to ensure reliable use by learners and institutional partners. The developer will translate existing VSP features into a stable, production-ready system, while also contributing to broader technology development, infrastructure setup, and technical support activities within the SHN Research Institute (SHNRI).\\nResponsibilities:\\n· Develop features end-to-end across the frontend, backend, data layer, and agents.\\n· Build and improve the real-time, voice-API-powered conversational patient interactions, optimizing for latency, reliability, and quality.\\n· Strengthen the AI assessment pipeline by developing LLM-driven audio/video and rubric analysis tools backed by validated evaluation frameworks.\\n· Design for scale by refining permissions, multi-tenant architectures, administrative workflows, and data security/privacy standards.\\n· Manage cloud infrastructure and DevOps pipelines including AWS, database migrations, deployments, and CI/CD environments.\\n· Build usage tracking, metering, and consumption analytics to support billing and capacity planning.\\n· Support technical scoping and translate product requirements into engineering roadmaps.\\n· Assist in the setup and maintenance of hardware- and software-related infrastructure within SHNRI, including GPU configuration and AI workflow integrations.\\n· Collaborate with IT and Cybersecurity teams to ensure institutional compliance, data protection, and platform security.\\n· Adhere to strict technical standards, including standard Git workflows, code reviews, quality assurance, end-to-end testing, and observability.\\n· Maintain up-to-date system documentation, logs of activities, and technical materials.\\n· Work cross-functionally with designers, research coordinators, and business development teams to clarify requirements.\\n· Performs other duties and provide administrative support as assigned and required.\\nRequirements:\\n· Undergraduate Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\\n· Minimum of 3 years of full-stack software engineering experience.\\n· Advanced proficiency in Python and Python-based API frameworks.\\n· Advanced proficiency in database management with PostgreSQL or compatible managed services (Supabase, Neon, AWS RDS).\\n· Advanced experience in building authentication, role-based access control, Single Sign-On (SSO), and multi-tenant architectures.\\n· Advanced experience in end-to-end testing, debugging, system monitoring, and production support.\\n· Advanced proficiency in using AI-assisted coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex) to augment engineering velocity without sacrificing code quality.\\n· Advanced communication, project management, and problem-solving skills with high agency and initiative.\\n· Intermediate experience with React, Next.js, and modern frontend frameworks.\\n· Intermediate experience with AWS or similar cloud infrastructure platforms and DevOps practices.\\n· Intermediate experience working in cross-functional teams with designers, product managers, and researchers.\\n· Basic knowledge of graphic design and UI/UX engineering tools (such as Figma).\\nAssets:\\n· Master’s Degree in Computer Science or a related engineering domain.\\n· Prior experience developing voice-agent APIs, real-time streaming tools, or healthcare technology applications.\\nAccommodation and Diversity Statement:\\nScarborough Health Network (SHN) embraces and celebrates our community’s unique multicultural heritage and diversity. SHN is an equal opportunity employer, dedicated to a culture of inclusiveness and diversity reflecting our diverse patients, staff and community alike. \\n\\nWe are committed to fostering an environment of equity and inclusivity where every person can work and receive care safely, openly and honestly. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, nation of origin, genetics, disability, age, veteran status, marital or family status, belief system, or other factors related to one’s personal identity and/or values. \\n\\nWe are committed to providing barrier-free and accessible employment practices in compliance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). Should you require accommodation through any stage of the recruitment process, please make them known when contacted and we will work with you to meet your needs.\\nLearn more about our exciting opportunities by following SHNCareers on Instagram, Twitter, and Facebook.\",\"frontend_payload\":{\"about_company\":[\"Across our three hospitals and eight satellite sites, Scarborough Health Network (SHN) is shaping the future of care. Our many programs and services are designed around the needs of one of Canada’s most vibrant and diverse communities. We are home to North America’s largest nephrology program, as well as the designated cardiac care and spine centre for Scarborough and surrounding communities to the east. We are proud to be a community-affiliated teaching site for the University of Toronto and partner with a number of other universities and colleges, helping to train the next generation of health care professionals. SHN is the recipient of the 2021 Excellence in Diversity and Inclusion Award, from the Canadian College of Health Leaders, for our leading edge work on Communities of Inclusion, Inclusion Calendar, Health Equity Certificate Program and much more. We are also proud to be named Canada’s Most Admired Corporate Cultures for 2023 and 2024! Learn more at shn.ca\"],\"about_role\":\"The Software Developer will primarily support the implementation and ongoing development of the Virtual Standardized Patient (VSP) platform within a college training environment. This position focuses on integrating, deploying, testing, maintaining, and enhancing the platform and its supporting services to ensure reliable use by learners and institutional partners. The developer will translate existing VSP features into a stable, production-ready system, while also contributing to broader technology development, infrastructure setup, and technical support activities within the SHN Research Institute (SHNRI).\",\"annual_salary\":[\"$51.427 - $59.618 per hour\"],\"benefits\":[],\"education_level\":[\"Undergraduate Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\",\"Master’s Degree in Computer Science or a related engineering domain.\"],\"equal_opportunity\":[\"Scarborough Health Network (SHN) embraces and celebrates our community’s unique multicultural heritage and diversity. SHN is an equal opportunity employer, dedicated to a culture of inclusiveness and diversity reflecting our diverse patients, staff and community alike.\",\"We are committed to fostering an environment of equity and inclusivity where every person can work and receive care safely, openly and honestly.\",\"All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, nation of origin, genetics, disability, age, veteran status, marital or family status, belief system, or other factors related to one’s personal identity and/or values.\",\"We are committed to providing barrier-free and accessible employment practices in compliance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). Should you require accommodation through any stage of the recruitment process, please make them known when contacted and we will work with you to meet your needs.\"],\"experience_level\":[\"Minimum of 3 years of full-stack software engineering experience\",\"Advanced proficiency\",\"Intermediate experience\",\"Basic knowledge\"],\"location\":[\"Centenary Site\"],\"requirements\":[\"Undergraduate Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\",\"Minimum of 3 years of full-stack software engineering experience.\",\"Advanced proficiency in Python and Python-based API frameworks.\",\"Advanced proficiency in database management with PostgreSQL or compatible managed services (Supabase, Neon, AWS RDS).\",\"Advanced experience in building authentication, role-based access control, Single Sign-On (SSO), and multi-tenant architectures.\",\"Advanced experience in end-to-end testing, debugging, system monitoring, and production support.\",\"Advanced proficiency in using AI-assisted coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex) to augment engineering velocity without sacrificing code quality.\",\"Advanced communication, project management, and problem-solving skills with high agency and initiative.\",\"Intermediate experience with React, Next.js, and modern frontend frameworks.\",\"Intermediate experience with AWS or similar cloud infrastructure platforms and DevOps practices.\",\"Intermediate experience working in cross-functional teams with designers, product managers, and researchers.\",\"Basic knowledge of graphic design and UI/UX engineering tools (such as Figma).\"],\"responsibilities\":[\"Develop features end-to-end across the frontend, backend, data layer, and agents.\",\"Build and improve real-time, voice-API-powered conversational patient interactions, optimizing for latency, reliability, and quality.\",\"Strengthen the AI assessment pipeline by developing LLM-driven audio/video and rubric analysis tools backed by validated evaluation frameworks.\",\"Design for scale by refining permissions, multi-tenant architectures, administrative workflows, and data security/privacy standards.\",\"Manage cloud infrastructure and DevOps pipelines including AWS, database migrations, deployments, and CI/CD environments.\",\"Build usage tracking, metering, and consumption analytics to support billing and capacity planning.\",\"Support technical scoping and translate product requirements into engineering roadmaps.\",\"Assist in the setup and maintenance of hardware- and software-related infrastructure within SHNRI, including GPU configuration and AI workflow integrations.\",\"Collaborate with IT and Cybersecurity teams to ensure institutional compliance, data protection, and platform security.\",\"Adhere to strict technical standards, including standard Git workflows, code reviews, quality assurance, end-to-end testing, and observability.\",\"Maintain up-to-date system documentation, logs of activities, and technical materials.\",\"Work cross-functionally with designers, research coordinators, and business development teams to clarify requirements.\",\"Perform other duties and provide administrative support as assigned and required.\"],\"skills\":[\"Python\",\"Python-based API frameworks\",\"PostgreSQL\",\"Supabase\",\"Neon\",\"AWS RDS\",\"Authentication\",\"Role-based access control\",\"Single Sign-On (SSO)\",\"Multi-tenant architectures\",\"End-to-end testing\",\"Debugging\",\"System monitoring\",\"Production support\",\"AI-assisted coding tools\",\"Claude Code\",\"Cursor\",\"Codex\",\"React\",\"Next.js\",\"AWS\",\"DevOps practices\",\"Graphic design\",\"UI/UX engineering tools\",\"Figma\",\"Voice-agent APIs\",\"Real-time streaming tools\",\"Healthcare technology applications\"],\"work_type\":[\"Temporary (Fixed Term)\",\"Full time\"]}},{\"id\":\"7f4a5f8a-da06-47b0-a561-607a4a059074\",\"source_id\":\"2421651616\",\"obfuscated_id\":42525967,\"title\":\"Software Developer\",\"organization\":\"Winsupply\",\"job_url\":\"https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/Winsupply1/3743990016221166-software-developer\",\"employment_type\":null,\"date_posted\":\"2026-10-19T15:15:20.218181Z\",\"locations_derived\":[\"Moraine, OH, US\",\"Moraine, OH, USA\",\"Moraine, OH, United States\",\"Moraine, Ohio, US\",\"Moraine, Ohio, USA\",\"Moraine, Ohio, United States\",\"OH, US\",\"OH, USA\",\"OH, United States\",\"Ohio, US\",\"Ohio, USA\",\"Ohio, United States\",\"US\",\"USA\",\"United States\"],\"cities_derived\":null,\"countries_derived\":null,\"remote_derived\":false,\"company_id\":\"e579d3ea-e773-b0f7-4022-8d57b2da8226\",\"company_image_id\":\"v1491017527/suq2whdxilunnz9orgoq.png\",\"logo\":\"\",\"salary_currency\":\"\",\"salary_min_value\":0,\"salary_max_value\":0,\"salary_unit_text\":\"\",\"ai_salary_currency\":\"USD\",\"ai_salary_min_value\":75000,\"ai_salary_max_value\":110000,\"ai_salary_unit_text\":\"yearly\",\"ai_key_skills\":[\"Java\",\"Spring Boot\",\"Angular\",\"IBM DB2\",\"RESTful APIs\",\"Microservices\",\"Gradle\",\"CI/CD\",\"Jenkins\",\"Docker\",\"Kubernetes\",\"Agile\",\"Jira\",\"SQL\",\"Test-driven development\"],\"experience_level\":\"\",\"work_arrangement\":\"\",\"description_text\":\"Company Description\\nWinsupply is in the business of creating and enabling entrepreneurs to achieve their dreams through wholesale distribution. Winsupply is a group of over 680 locally-owned companies that operate across a variety of industries, including HVAC, Plumbing, Electrical and more. The purpose of the support services campus is to eliminate obstacles and provide support to help our entrepreneurs succeed. Support service employees assist entrepreneurs in achieving their dreams through finance, accounting, IT, and other back-office operations.\\nJob Description\\nPosition Summary\\nThe Intermediate FullStack Developer will serve as the subject matter expert for Java and web services, applying industry best practices in software development and agile project management. Lead assigned development and integration projects from inception to delivery. Collaborate with business users to define requirements, create conceptual and technical designs, develop prototypes and programs, execute unit and integration tests, resolve defects, implement solutions, and provide second-tier support. Champion innovation, continuous improvement, and technical excellence across the team.\\nCompetencies for Success\\nStrong organizational, analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.\\nStrong interpersonal skills to effectively collaborate with stakeholders at all levels.\\nMentor and guide junior developers, ensuring skill development and adherence to emerging technologies and best practices.\\nStay updated on new technologies and continuously enhance your technical skills.\\nTechnology Stack\\nBackend: Java (8 and newer), Spring Boot framework.\\nBuild Tool: Gradle.\\nDatabase: IBM DB2 LUW as the primary database.\\nFrontend: Angular framework.\\nCommunication: Message Queues (MQs).\\nTools and Methodologies: Agile (Scrum), Jira for task tracking, Confluence for documentation.\\nDevOps: CI/CD pipelines with Jenkins, containerization with Docker or Kubernetes.\\nMonitoring: ELK stack, Prometheus, Grafana.\\nQualifications\\nRequired Skills and Experiences\\n3+ years of professional IT experience, including service development using Java.\\nBachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent experience.\\nProven experience working with offshore development teams.\\nComprehensive understanding of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), distributed programming, multi-tier application design, and multi-threaded development.\\nActively participate in the software development lifecycle, including test-driven development, automated unit testing, and pair programming.\\nExperience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud) is a plus.\\nImplement DevOps processes, including CI/CD scripting, test automation, and containerization.\\nExperience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud) is a plus.\\nFamiliarity with monitoring and logging tools such as ELK stack, Prometheus, or Grafana.\\nProficiency in design patterns, RESTful services implementation, and service-oriented architectures.\\nKnowledge of test-driven development (TDD) and acceptance testing frameworks.\\nExpertise in development with Java 8 or newer, Spring Boot framework, and JPA.\\nHands-on experience with Gradle as a build tool.\\nProficiency in developing efficient, scalable RESTful web services and microservices.\\nFamiliarity with Domain-Driven Design (DDD) principles.\\nKnowledge of message queues (MQs) for inter-service communication.\\nSolid experience with version control tools such as GitHub.\\nAgile methodology experience, particularly in Scrum with bi-weekly sprints.\\nExperience with task tracking using Jira and documentation in Confluence.\\nStrong understanding of recognized Java Design Patterns.\\nPractical experience with relational databases (preferably IBM DB2 LUW), including writing moderate to complex SQL queries.\\nFront-end development exposure using Angular framework is a plus.\\nExperience with designing and implementing highly available and fault-tolerant systems.\\nFamiliarity with performance optimization techniques for both backend and frontend.\\nCollaborate with technical teams to design and deliver scalable, effective solutions that align with business requirements.\\nDevelop and maintain RESTful APIs, microservices, and other service-oriented architectures.\\nAdhere to best practices and standards for accessibility, cross-browser compatibility, and security.\\nWork with cross-functional teams, including project managers, UI/UX designers, developers, and architects, to ensure consistent and high-quality deliverables.\\nOperate efficiently in Linux shell environments and perform necessary configurations.\\nUtilize Jenkins or similar tools to automate builds and deployments.\\nConduct thorough code reviews and integration testing to ensure quality and maintainability.\\nEngage in the requirement specification process for new software functionalities, ensuring design consistency with development standards.\\nChampion the adoption of engineering best practices and promote a culture of continuous learning and improvement.\\nDevelop technical documentation, including architectural designs and guidelines, to ensure long-term maintainability.\\nTake ownership of the end-to-end development cycle, from design to deployment and monitoring in production environments.\\nDrive efforts to improve application performance, scalability, and reliability.\\nAdditional Information\\nPhysical Demands\\nThe physical demands here are representative of those that must be met to successfully perform the essential job functions with or without reasonable accommodations:\\nEmployee is regularly required to sit, use hands, handle controls, talk and hear, reach with hands and arms, stand, walk and stoop.\\nVision requirements include close vision and ability to focus\\nWe are committed to inclusion, diversity, and equal employment opportunity, regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, gender, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.\"}],\"total_items\":400,\"total_pages\":34},\"message\":\"success\"}"
